{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_0","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc 'rg -n -A 35 -B 8 \"A senior analyst.s granularity|D248\" AGENTS.md docs/DECISIONS-log.md'","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_0","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc 'rg -n -A 35 -B 8 \"A senior analyst.s granularity|D248\" AGENTS.md docs/DECISIONS-log.md'","aggregated_output":"AGENTS.md-115-  writer and delete its duplicate implementations in the same change; when a fix lands in one consumer, search every consumer of the\nAGENTS.md-116-  same key or rule.\nAGENTS.md-117-- **Code over prose.** A contract that code or a schema can enforce (an enum over allowed keys, a shape) is enforced there, and stays out\nAGENTS.md-118-  of prompts and documents.\nAGENTS.md-119-- **One word per concept.** The glossary in `docs/prd/00-system.md` (section Glossary; D36, D163) names each concept once, and\nAGENTS.md-120-  `docs/check.py` fails on a word it rules out. A new concept gets its row and its ruled-out words in the same change; a new ruled-out\nAGENTS.md-121-  word must catch the sentence it was written against and pass the corrected one.\nAGENTS.md-122-- **Identity.** An identifier names one thing for the life of its scope; a changed thing gets a new id. Equal values alone never\nAGENTS.md:123:  establish identity (D248 boundary 7, the same statement carried by several outlets, is a chosen exception, switched on only after its\nAGENTS.md-124-  merge risk on the gold and the accuracy of the original speaker and day fields are measured).\nAGENTS.md-125-- **Explicit inputs.** Library code takes runtime paths and configuration as arguments. A branch a run takes comes from its\nAGENTS.md-126-  configuration, never from whether an environment variable happens to be set; a configured step whose credential is missing refuses\nAGENTS.md-127-  the run. A component that sends a model call uses the transport its caller passes.\nAGENTS.md-128-- **Never order by the wall clock.** It steps both ways; order comes from a sequence the program owns: dispatch's sequence number. The\nAGENTS.md-129-  stream never reads the calendar; only pull mode acts on time, with its \"now\" passed in (D12, D13, D31).\nAGENTS.md-130-- **Strictness is code too.** A check added to prevent defects can itself fail; accept it on real data, not samples.\nAGENTS.md-131-- **Style.** Descriptive names. Docstrings and comments state behaviour, not history. The standard library unless a measured need\nAGENTS.md-132-  justifies a dependency.\nAGENTS.md-133-- **Frontend presentation.** Follow the sentence-case and metadata-separator rules in `docs/poc/thesis-ui.md#presentation-rules`.\nAGENTS.md-134-\nAGENTS.md-135-## 4. Tests\nAGENTS.md-136-\nAGENTS.md-137-- Every test names the requirement or table row it proves; a test that traces to none is deleted, and a retired behaviour's tests leave\nAGENTS.md-138-  with it. The suite stays lean.\nAGENTS.md-139-- Before writing a test, read every function its fixture drives: return shapes, failure classification, the data and attributes it\nAGENTS.md-140-  reads. Check that a name exists before calling it.\nAGENTS.md-141-- Real objects first (real storage on a temporary path, real records). Fake only external services (a model client, a data source, an\nAGENTS.md-142-  HTTP server). Fixture values are realistic (real ISO timestamps, not placeholders).\nAGENTS.md-143-- Tests never reach a paid service or load a credential: `tests/conftest.py` replaces the model and Jev key readers with a refusal, so a\nAGENTS.md-144-  call that escapes its fake transport fails the test.\nAGENTS.md-145-- Write the one decisive assertion that fails without the code under test, and predict the run before running it. A first failure for\nAGENTS.md-146-  any other reason means the test was written blind: stop and read again. A test is never mended to fit the code; it changes only when\nAGENTS.md-147-  the spec changes, and the spec change is recorded first.\nAGENTS.md-148-- Mutate on a scratch copy: the test must fail on the mutant while the unmutated control passes. An error is not a catch until its\nAGENTS.md-149-  traceback is read. A negative assertion (\"never called\") needs a mutant that makes the call on the tested path.\nAGENTS.md-150-- A check must judge something: it reports how many cases it judged, carries a positive control that fails for the breach it holds, and\nAGENTS.md-151-  fails when its own preconditions fail (exit status, a missing or unidentifiable input). A check over an empty population is\nAGENTS.md-152-  unexercised, not passed.\nAGENTS.md-153-- Tests never depend on the real date or the working directory: pin every date written and read, build paths from the test file's\nAGENTS.md-154-  location, write only inside temporary directories.\nAGENTS.md-155-- Test each entry point as its user calls it (with the defaults the user leaves unset, under the configuration the user runs), not only\nAGENTS.md-156-  the inner function with every argument set.\nAGENTS.md-157-\nAGENTS.md-158-## 5. Verification\n--\nAGENTS.md-226-\nAGENTS.md-227-## 7. Measuring and iterating\nAGENTS.md-228-\nAGENTS.md-229-### 7.1 The ruler\nAGENTS.md-230-\nAGENTS.md-231-- **One ruler.** Every gold, judge, prompt and acceptance uses the one standard named before the first arm. A second ruler in use (an old\nAGENTS.md-232-  reference, a judge's rubric, a prompt's own categories) is a defect, fixed before anything is measured (D241, Alex: \"我们今天一直浪费时间在不同标准之间来回\").\nAGENTS.md-233-- **The frozen ruler (D261, D262; 2026-11-02)** remains the standard for existing measurements and historical comparisons until a separately reviewed replacement is established. For future evidence scoring (D372), combine the existing gold's core and supporting as helpful, treat its not-kept entries as unhelpful, and leave optional entries neutral; this does not alter the frozen files. Its pieces, with the hashes code checks:\nAGENTS.md:234:  1. The extraction standard: `docs/prd/05-extraction-standard.html`, its version 5 (version 3 as signed in D243, with D248's seven\nAGENTS.md-235-     boundaries and D250's four evidence boundaries and counting unit); the gold `docs/research/2026-10-29-ledger-standard/golden-v5/` (dev sha256 `6f9476bb…`, test `af2145cd…`, recorded\nAGENTS.md-236-     in `golden-v5.sha256`). There is no version 6.\nAGENTS.md-237-  2. The questions: golden-v5's must_open / may_open (questions standard version 3) and the seeds `poc/seeds/nvda-2026-07-01-v2.json`\nAGENTS.md-238-     (`fca16f42…`, 22 questions). The seeds are part of the ruler: the judgement scorer refuses a run whose seed questions differ; a new\nAGENTS.md-239-     seed set is a new ruler version, opened only by Alex's decision.\nAGENTS.md-240-  3. The judgement ruler (D3): `docs/research/2026-11-01-e2e-loop/judgement-gold/`: `ruler-v1.md` (the definition), `reader-brief.md`,\nAGENTS.md-241-     `packet-v1.json` (golden-v5's 309 items, `53d1e8b4…`), `questions-v1.json` (the 22 seeds plus the Ohio guarantee, `30854180…`),\nAGENTS.md-242-     `gold-v1.json` = reader B's answers (`636c056d…`, in `gold-v1.sha256`), `score_judgement.py` (refuses any other sha256 or ruler\nAGENTS.md-243-     version), `corrections-v1.json` (dated records only, printed with every score, never merged).\nAGENTS.md-244-\nAGENTS.md-245-  None of these files changes again (`tests/test_frozen_rulers.py` fails the suite when a hash moves; Alex, 2026-11-02: \"你的尺子做出来和金标真的不能再动了，\nAGENTS.md-246-  已经造成了3天的各种漂移，非常的严重 … 我们做完的review过的尺子金标不能再动了\"). A defect found later is a dated correction record beside the gold,\nAGENTS.md-247-  with its reason and its before and after, printed with every score and never merged in. Every measurement names the gold version it used. A new piece (the D2\nAGENTS.md-248-  matter-to-question mapping, not yet built, is one) is an addition recorded as such, never an edit of these. A new version of any piece\nAGENTS.md-249-  exists only by Alex's decision, derives its gold from scratch, and old scores are never compared with it. A disagreement between the\nAGENTS.md-250-  system and the gold is a gap in the system to close (D263), never a case for the ruler. A suspected inconsistency between gold and\nAGENTS.md-251-  standard no longer stops an arm: record the concern separately, continue scoring on the unchanged frozen gold, and disclose it with the results (D373).\nAGENTS.md-252-  What it measures: extraction against the gold's items, questions against must_open / may_open, the judgement at the window end\nAGENTS.md-253-  2026-07-14 against reader B's ranges (a numeric question agrees when the gold range overlaps the chosen rung's band, a yes/no question\nAGENTS.md-254-  when the answers match). What it does not measure: the judgement's daily path, and whether evidence was filed under the right question.\nAGENTS.md-255-- **The extraction standard** (piece 1) is the extraction step's PRD, signed by Alex on 2026-10-29 (D243: \"其他几条的意见我都ok，sign off\"),\nAGENTS.md-256-  which replaced the first version (D229: \"按照这套标准来开始做测量，这条标准不要漂移\"). It holds the ledger's three records, the five question\nAGENTS.md-257-  types, the opening tests, the evidence rule and its reject list, source tiers, weight, and how a prompt change is written, measured and\nAGENTS.md-258-  iterated. No arm, gold, judge or prompt adds a rule, an example or a weight the page does not hold; a change is a recorded decision in\nAGENTS.md-259-  Alex's words first, then a new version of the page, then a drift review.\nAGENTS.md-260-- **A ruler or gold that is built and reviewed is never changed again** (D261). Reviewed means readers who did not write it have read it\nAGENTS.md-261-  against the decisions and Alex has signed it. A ruler under construction is edited only until that review, and nothing is scored\nAGENTS.md-262-  against it before.\nAGENTS.md-263-- **The ruler is Alex's, never your own.** Gold, unit and the judge's reading are checked against what the product uses and fixed with\nAGENTS.md-264-  Alex before the first arm. A standard or reference you write gives every sentence its source (the signed standard, a decision, a PRD)\nAGENTS.md-265-  or lists it for Alex's decision with a lean; settling wording is no licence to change behaviour. After each rewrite, a read-only Codex\nAGENTS.md-266-  review against the decisions looks for unsourced rules, contradictions and misquotes, round after round until only wording-level\nAGENTS.md-267-  findings remain; clarity is tested apart, by independent readers on cases fixed before the text changes. A failed registered acceptance\nAGENTS.md-268-  stops the line and goes to Alex with its census; the next arm is never designed alone.\nAGENTS.md-269-- **Nobody grades their own change with a ruler still being corrected.** The reference is one Alex can read, reviewed and frozen before\n--\nAGENTS.md-374-\nAGENTS.md-375-- Think like a hedge-fund analyst. A thesis is an argued view about the business and the world; its stance comes from the argument\nAGENTS.md-376-  weighed against what is priced. Extract the few metrics or segments that carry it; financial-statement lines are its evidence, never its\nAGENTS.md-377-  definition.\nAGENTS.md-378-- **Lean cautious, catch the increment.** Most of what an item says is noise: not everything is evidence and not everything is a lead. A\nAGENTS.md-379-  typical claim or background line is common knowledge (what an analyst following the company knew before the item) and is not kept\nAGENTS.md-380-  without a number and a specific narrative; new information that changes an answer is never missed. Alex, 2026-10-29 (D243):\nAGENTS.md-381-  \"不是什么事情都是惊弓之鸟需要抽取，杂音还是很大的，我们整体应该倾向谨慎不要看什么都是线索的感觉，但是同时我们要敏感一些新的信息带来的增量不要错过\".\nAGENTS.md:382:- **A senior analyst's granularity.** A question is a bet an analyst would hold a card for: a big matter, never trivia (a deal, product or\nAGENTS.md-383-  project opens one only when its scale can change revenue, profit, cash or credit risk). Small matters open no question, and whether\nAGENTS.md-384-  their statements are kept follows the evidence rule; wordings, deadlines, milestones and periods of one bet are one question, and a\nAGENTS.md-385-  statement carried by several outlets is one statement (how code applies it: §3, Identity). Two questions stay apart only when their answers can move apart and an analyst\nAGENTS.md:386:  would bet on each separately (D248). Alex, 2026-10-30: \"我觉得核心就是这个颗粒度的把控要符合一个高端的hedge fund analyst 的思维。不要搜集一堆鸡毛蒜皮的事情，要看重要的大事，合并整合关键的信息，这个是这个步骤的原则\".\nAGENTS.md-387-- The extraction standard (§7.1, piece 1) is the step's standard. Its two sources are applied before designing a prompt, evaluation or\nAGENTS.md-388-  change (D228): the thesis library's four evidence tiers (`docs/prd/06-views.md`, Four evidence tiers) and the investment-question\nAGENTS.md-389-  reasoning in the 90-thesis review (`research_notes/对冲基金论点粒度与金标/codex-challenger.md`, section 1; research, not a replacement for\nAGENTS.md-390-  recorded decisions). Source type and what a claim can support are separate judgments; no tier has a fixed score. Ask what revenue,\nAGENTS.md-391-  profitability, cash risk or competitive position the information can change; then separately decide whether it supports an existing\nAGENTS.md-392-  question or merits a new one. Indirect, incomplete and forecast information is evidence under the routing rules; none of those\nAGENTS.md-393-  properties, nor an inability to open a new question, alone makes it worthless.\nAGENTS.md-394-- Evaluate the overall research judgment against the source, the existing question and the evidence. Gold examples teach the reasoning\nAGENTS.md-395-  and its boundaries; reasonable alternative wording, evidence strength and inference are allowed (D226, D228). Record material factual\nAGENTS.md-396-  errors, unsupported assumptions and downstream losses separately. Do not turn a review's questions, output labels or optional details\nAGENTS.md-397-  into an automatic all-or-nothing score. Missing market expectations or historical context means that aspect was not tested, not that\nAGENTS.md-398-  it passed or failed.\nAGENTS.md-399-- When a thesis-quality check fails, look first at the unit of thought (are these the arguments that move the stock?), not deeper into\nAGENTS.md-400-  the numbers. Numbers are verified by code where they exist.\nAGENTS.md-401-- Outcomes are tracked and shown, never a gate on what a view may say. Missing data is \"no data to verify\", never a pass or a fail. A\nAGENTS.md-402-  repeat is not new evidence, and model agreement is not corroboration.\nAGENTS.md-403-\nAGENTS.md-404-## 9. Workspace and operations\nAGENTS.md-405-\nAGENTS.md-406-- Inspect a path before writing to it; new stored data gets a new, dated name; chain guarded steps with `&&`. Deleting stored data needs\nAGENTS.md-407-  Alex's request, a backup, exactly identified items and a log entry.\nAGENTS.md-408-- Absolute paths. Commands run under zsh: pass a list as an array. No foreground `sleep`.\nAGENTS.md-409-- Preserve existing and concurrent changes: never reset, clean or stash work that is not yours. Never run parallel agents that edit\nAGENTS.md-410-  shared modules.\nAGENTS.md-411-- When Alex names a step, the test is that step alone through its own harness (extraction: stored requests re-sent, answers sifted,\nAGENTS.md-412-  scored against the gold). A full-pipeline run, a registered test, or a paid send beyond the probes of a few cents an agreed direction\nAGENTS.md-413-  allows (§7.3) starts only on his explicit word (Alex, 2026-10-27: \"我不是要你看下step 1抽取到底行不行？\").\nAGENTS.md-414-- A long paid run is launched detached in a new session with a log and pid file, after checking machine and network health; nothing heavy\nAGENTS.md-415-  runs beside paid calls. A gate runs on a snapshot no one is editing.\nAGENTS.md-416-- Never open a live run's databases: run `sh <run folder>/snapshot.sh` and query the snapshot.\nAGENTS.md-417-- No edit to package code or prompt files while any run is live: the parallel day's manifest hashes every `.py` and prompt file and\nAGENTS.md-418-  fails the day. Edit in another worktree or wait.\nAGENTS.md-419-- Experiment harnesses send concurrently (a thread pool of 8; the archive is thread-safe); serial sends waste the wall clock Alex is\nAGENTS.md-420-  waiting on.\nAGENTS.md-421-- **Run settings** (`scripts/replay.py`): extraction requests prepared 16 at a time (`--workers`; the measurement launcher passes its\n--\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md-2946-- Decided: role-v51 replaces role-v42; `scripts/replay.py` defaults to `poc/config/poc-v67.json`, which differs from `poc-v58` only in the ten extraction prompt versions (T*-v51). role-v51 changes one clause of the main_driver opening reason to the page's §3 B row (the generation of the company's own product that carries the quantity, its launch or first shipment), with one example and one counter-example (+177 characters). Against role-v42 sent together: must-not questions on small products, features and services 20 → 0 over 15 draws each; one full run (development + test, three draws) shows no cost elsewhere: must-open raised in every draw 18 against 16 of 28, core 235 against 230 of 258, supporting in two draws 154 against 155 of 181, rejected sentences kept 100 against 106 per draw; all paired intervals cross 0 (`loop-log.md` rows 20–22).\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md-2947-\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md-2948-## D247 · 2026-10-30 · role-v53 (`poc-v69`) is the extraction request: the attribution fields are defined in the schema\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md-2949-\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md-2950-- Alex, on the report of the record-field class (\"默认换不换 v53\"): \"我们先锁定v53吧。\"\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md-2951-- Decided: `scripts/replay.py` defaults to `poc/config/poc-v69.json`, which differs from `poc-v67` only in the ten extraction prompt versions (T*-v53). role-v53's role text is role-v51's unchanged; from version 53 the schema carries descriptions of `speaker`, `original_who` and `original_day` (`extraction.FIELD_NOTES`; standard 5.4 and 5.5, D203, D220, the signed gold's who column), and every earlier version's schema is byte-identical (`tests/test_field_notes.py`).\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md-2952-- Measured (`loop-log.md` rows 26–33, `research/2026-10-29-ledger-standard/fields-2026-10-30/`): writing the same definitions into the role text (role-v52) fixed the fields but kept about 7–15 more gold-rejected statements per draw; in the schema, against role-v51 sent together (run U, development + test, three draws): outlet-as-speaker and report-day signals 166 → 35 over 148 articles × 3 draws; verified field errors on a blind read of 24 fresh articles 18/96 → 11/94 records; gold-rejected statements kept −6.7 per draw; core per draw −1.3 and supporting at least two draws −4, both inside their paired intervals; must-open raised in every draw 17 → 22. Two follow-ups did not beat it and are not adopted: role-v54 (the role text's attribution clause removed) and role-v55 (the tier rule moved to the schema, refuted on its small sample). Left open: an author's restatement of another company's reported figures is still credited to the author (role-v56, which removes the T7 and T8 attribution phrases, is built and unsent).\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md-2953-\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:2954:## D248 · 2026-10-30 · What counts as one question and one piece of evidence: seven boundaries, chosen one by one\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md-2955-\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md-2956-- Alex, on the census of duplicate and trivial questions: \"我们的标准要收口\"; then \"你要不要深度的写好plan, 怎么测量，golden 是怎么，我们来解决这个问题；整体不能regress，你要秉持我们过往工程的原则，以及作为一个hedge fund analyst 到底怎么判断合并，去重，这个标准很重要，不能观点爆炸\"; then, not following the plan's table, \"我没理解每个难点，我需要一个一个和你过，你讲人话给我例子\". Each boundary was put to him with an example and two options; his replies are quoted per row. Plan, census and review rounds: [question-identity plan](research/2026-10-30-question-identity/plan.md) §0–§4, §11b, §12.\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md-2957-- The class ($0, `census/`): the sealed three-month run opened 69 questions in 59 days; Claude's reading of the first 50 (not reviewed by Alex) marks 12 duplicates and 10 that should not have opened, 5 borderline. Matching merged 39 of 122 candidates; the candidates opened new fall in three verdict classes (parsed from the decisions' reason text, not yet verified case by case): the collision judge's \"distinct question in one matter\", \"same question\" verdicts the code still opened (two traced to a model-written period start), and twins never compared.\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:2958:- The principle, Alex after the seven answers: \"我觉得核心就是这个颗粒度的把控要符合一个高端的hedge fund analyst 的思维。不要搜集一堆鸡毛蒜皮的事情，要看重要的大事，合并整合关键的信息，这个是这个步骤的原则\" (written into AGENTS §8, \"A senior analyst's granularity\").\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md-2959-- Decided (the general rule under all seven: two questions are one when the same outcome settles both; they are kept apart only when their answers can move apart and an analyst would bet on each separately):\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md-2960-  1. **One plan, several wordings** (H1, \"A\"): wordings of one plan whose final check is the same number are one question; two numbers that move on their own and are watched separately stay apart; a single deal under a plan already opened by amount merges into it. Not put to Alex: a not-yet-signed deal's yes/no signing question (D210; PRD 06 keeps number and event questions apart) stays as it is and does not merge into a plan's amount question (the Ohio lease guarantee and the cloud-customer total in v38 both stay). Narrows the standard §4 \"another quantity in the same deal (a guarantee beside a financing)\" sentence taken from D190; consistent with D210.\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md-2961-  2. **One event, several deadlines** (H2, \"A\"): while the earlier-deadline question is open, a later deadline is its evidence, not a new question; when the earlier one falls due unresolved and the matter is still live, the system opens the next-deadline successor with the merged evidence, without waiting for a new article (new work for pull mode, D14, D54).\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md-2962-  3. **One product generation, several milestones** (H3, \"A\"): one question per generation, asked at the step that brings revenue (shipments begin); sampling and launch are its evidence; only milestones an analyst bets on separately (a drug's phase-3 data and its approval) are separate questions.\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md-2963-  4. **A company's own quantity by fiscal and by calendar year** (H4, \"A\"): only the fiscal year opens (PRD 06 ladder rule 5); a calendar-year estimate is evidence to the fiscal question, weighed lower when the years differ much.\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md-2964-  5. **A model-written period start** (H5, \"A\"): for event and policy questions it no longer blocks a merge; object, event and due day are still checked.\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md-2965-  6. **Small matters opened as questions** (H6, \"A， A\"): a deal, product or project (the question was put about small deals and products) opens a question only when its scale can change the company's revenue, profit, cash or credit risk; otherwise no question opens, and whether its statement is kept follows the evidence rule (standard §5). Done in this round together with the merge changes, each measured as its own arm, then together on the holdout. Narrows the standard §3 class C (\"a sized, not yet completed stake or acquisition\").\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md-2966-  7. **The same statement carried by several outlets** (H7, \"A\"): code treats pieces with the same known original speaker, original day and figures as one (an unknown speaker or day never matches: 297 of the sealed run's 4,298 pieces have both unknown); the judge sees it once with the outlet count; every piece is still stored. Changes D204's \"both shown to the judge\" for this case, and is a chosen exception to AGENTS §3 \"equal values alone never establish identity\"; the risk put to him with the question (a qualification such as \"excluding China sales\" hidden; D204's 8 of 40 wrong merges) is measured on the G3 gold before it is switched on, as is the accuracy of the original-speaker and original-day fields it relies on.\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md-2967-- Next, in this order: the signed standard page (§3 class C, §4 \"same question, succession or another question\") carries these rules, then a read-only Codex drift review; then the plan's step 1 (structured census, the fixed-extraction replay harness, gold G1–G3, the September holdout week on Alex's go).\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md-2968-\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md-2969-## D249 · 2026-10-30 · A test the model applies to each statement is a check at the end of the same request; role-v63 (`poc-v79`) measured, the default stays role-v53\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md-2970-\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md-2971-- Alex, after a second-turn probe judged statements by standard 5.1 correctly that the one-pass answer had kept: \"那为什么你不在prompt 里面要求做完自己复核一边就好，这样就是一个call完成\"; then \"你尝试一组先吧，这个完全就是再prompt 的最后面要求做完一遍基于\"你刚才说的复核条件\"再跑一次；写在同一个提示词里面\"; then \"可以，但是这个做法是有效的对吧，那你应该好好地写复核的侧重点然后跑；这个如果有效可以记录下来这个做法\"; then the goal \"你需要让这个加到prompt里面的方式improve performance. 一定要improve but don't hardcode or break our principles\".\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md-2972-- Decided (the method, written at AGENTS §6): from role-v59 the extraction request ends with a check that reads the evidence list back by standard 5.1 (`prompts/review-v<N>.txt`, `extraction.REVIEW_FROM`) and names no empty-answer condition; the role text of role-v59 to role-v63 is role-v53's. Every line of the check cites the standard (§5.1, §5.3, §6, D238, D243, D240); six read-only Codex rounds (`research/2026-10-30-noise/codex-review-*`); examples from other industries.\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md-2973-- Measured (run Y3, role-v53 and role-v63 sent together, development 118 + test 30 articles, three draws; `loop-log.md` rows 34–48): gold-rejected statements kept per draw 94.3 → 77.3 (−17, interval −33 to −2); core kept in every draw 72 → 74 of 86 and supporting in at least two draws 152 → 154 of 181 once a blind reader judged the 58 entries the counting aid scored differently (core draws 31 → 34, supporting 85 → 85); test supporting in at least two draws 38 → 41 of 42.\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md-2974-- Not decided: switching the default to `poc-v79`. Alex's reply to the report was \"你可以commit push\", with further noise work asked (\"但是还是有70多篇被留下\"), not an answer to the switch; `scripts/replay.py` stays on `poc-v69`.\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md-2975-\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md-2976-## D250 · 2026-10-31 · Four evidence boundaries and the counting unit settled; the ruler is fixed before any further measurement (standard version 5)\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md-2977-\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md-2978-- Alex, on the ruler check of the not-kept statements role-v63 keeps (`research/2026-10-30-noise/ruler-check-2026-10-31.md`; a blind reader agreed with the gold on 93–95% of the controls and on 70% of the entries v63 kept) and the five places put to him with a lean each: \"五处都按你的倾向定，计数单位也改; 你要修正尺子；你已经多次因为尺子标准问题陷入假的测量\".\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md-2979-- Decided (each is the lean he was given):\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md-2980-  1. **An arrangement retold without a new step** (Nokia AI-RAN collaboration, a carmaker's model on the platform, labs using a system): the lean as put: \"只描述一个现成安排、没有新动作的，算背景，不收\". An arrangement the item only describes as already in place (a collaboration, a customer using a product, a deployment), with no new step, is background and not kept, even when the item gives no date; everything else under the retelling row (D243 item 6, \"看不出是旧事的不算重提\") is judged as before, and guidance and a forecast or plan still in force keep their weight when retold.\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md-2981-  2. **How close another company's matter must be** (a lidar maker's price cut, a partner's reactor going critical): the lean as put: \"说不出它通过需求、供给、竞争、定价这类路径动了英伟达哪个问题的，不收\". Another company's matter that one cannot say moves a question about the company through a path such as demand, supply, competition or pricing is not kept; a party next to the company only by sharing an article, an event or an ecosystem is not kept.\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md-2982-  3. **A comparison the company, a partner or a third party publishes** (\"10x lower cost than closed models\", \"40% more GPUs in the same power budget\", a third party's test): the lean as put: \"标准只说'对手拿来和本公司比'的要按 5.1 判；其余的都算产品细节，不收\". A partner's or customer's adoption or integration in the same sentence is not dropped by this rule and is judged by 5.1 as before (the lean says nothing about it; an unconditional keep would be a new rule); ruling 4 (a competitor's 2.4x, supporting) unchanged.\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md-2983-  4. **A named analyst's view of a new event** (\"a Kyber delay widens the window for alternatives\"): the lean as put: \"只是解读一件已经记下的事、没有新事实或推算的，不收\". One that adds a new fact or calculation is judged by 5.1; the conditional valuation (5.3) is unchanged.\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md-2984-  5. **The counting unit**: the lean as put: \"只有当那条记录本身不是该留的事，才算留了杂音\". A not-kept gold entry counts as kept only when the record that carries it is not itself the same matter as a core, supporting or optional gold entry (optional is never penalised); not-kept words that ride inside the quote of a kept matter are one record of that matter (\"一件事用几句话说仍是一条\", standard §2).\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:2985:- The ruler (Alex: \"你要修正尺子\"): the standard page goes to version 5 with these rules, then a read-only drift review; the gold's evidence part is re-derived for version 5 (version 4 changed no evidence entry, `gold-v4-evidence-check.md`) by two independent readers with every disagreement decided against the article, written as a new frozen file with every change listed (before, after, reason), the version-3 file untouched (D243 item 11); the opening part of the gold is not re-derived here and the scorer reports no question score until it is. The scorer refuses a gold whose evidence part was made for another version of the page: `final_scores.py` had bypassed `score_gold.py`'s version check and scored rounds since D248 on the version-3 gold, which is the false measurement Alex names.\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md-2986-- Not decided here: the financing-analysis entries (an IRR scenario, a debt-service floor) the blind reader would keep; they are judged by 5.1 in the re-derivation like any entry not on the 5.3 list.\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md-2987-\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md-2988-## D251 · 2026-10-31 · The extraction request may read the open questions as a daily snapshot (architecture under test)\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md-2989-\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md-2990-- Alex, on the reference-context architecture (`research/2026-10-31-reference-context/design.md`): extraction should \"read from the database and return all of the outstanding theses … as reference\", one line each, no evidence, so \"evidences can directly be linked to open theses\" and a new thesis is proposed only when none is open; on the open point of D211 (a request that changes with the ledger): \"是的每天为单位最快照读取\".\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md-2991-- Decided: when (and only when) the architecture is adopted after the measurement in design.md, the open-question list an extraction request shows is a snapshot frozen once per day; every article of that day sees the same list; the archive key is (item, snapshot hash); a day in flight never re-sends an item because the ledger moved. This narrows D211 (\"the request depends on the item alone\") to \"depends on the item and the day's snapshot\". Not decided: whether other companies' questions are shown, whether the one-home rule (D207) moves into the extraction prompt, what happens to a failed candidate's evidence; the measurement's predictions P1–P6 are frozen in design.md (sha256 in `predictions.sha256`).\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md-2992-\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md-2993-## D252 · 2026-10-31 · The extraction prompt teaches what noise looks like, with general paired counter-examples; useful theses and evidence must not regress\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md-2994-\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md-2995-- Alex, after the noise ruler was verified by two blind readers (130 of 165 kept gold-rejected entries confirmed noise) and four role versions showed noise and recall falling together on one line: \"you can probably start to add in some false positives on what in general should be considered as noise … we don't want to throw away the useful things in discovering key thesis. I think that is a very important metric. On top of that, it is whatever noise reduction that we can do … the hedge fund analyst has no idea in the prompts of what specifically constitute noise. And that's where I think in the prompt you should educate it … do not let this cause like regression to the extraction of useful theses … try not to make it like NVIDIA specific … a management statement that this is super bullish or whatever doesn't constitute as good evidence. It needs to be more evidence-based\".\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md-2996-- Decided: the role text carries a section that teaches noise by paired examples, one pair per §5.3 row that the measurement shows the model keeps (an existing arrangement retold against a new step; management cheer against guidance; an author's view against a sourced estimate; a trend remark against a figure; a product boast against business scale; a political stance against a policy step; a general risk against a supplier's stated cut; another company's own matter against one with a path; an analyst's reading against the fact it reads). Every pair is general (no covered company, product or figure) and sits inside its row's boundary: the kept side of each pair is what the standard keeps. The acceptance order is fixed: core and supporting recall first (no regression against the control, blind-corrected), then the noise count; a version that lowers recall is not adopted whatever its noise number.\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md-2997-- Not decided: the five proposals that would change the standard (P1–P5 in `research/2026-10-31-reference-context/design-v69.md`); they stay proposals.\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md-2998-\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md-2999-## D253 · 2026-10-31 · D208's first step is built: seed questions for a covered company, written before the run, as homes for evidence\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md-3000-\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md-3001-- Alex, after the end-to-end measurement and the reflection (`research/2026-10-31-reference-context/design-e2e.md`, `reflection-2026-10-31.md`: the placement call drops a third of the extracted core matters and 70% of the supporting ones for want of a question to file them under, while the questions those statements name — demand, inputs, competition and share, pricing, the company's own annual lines — are the root quantities and seven driver classes D208 designed and marked not built): the seed list for NVDA was put to him as a table (roots: FY2027 total revenue, data-center revenue, non-GAAP gross margin; drivers: hyperscaler capex 2026, server-memory contract price 2027, NVIDIA's share of 2026 data-center accelerator spending, the Rubin rack's price, Rubin shipping, China's H200 permission, AI Compute Partnership commitments). Alex: \"可以吧\".\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md-3002-- Decided: `scripts/replay.py --seed <file>` writes the seed questions into an empty ledger before the first day (views, ladders, keys, open switches, the driver's dependency on its root), from a per-company seed file the analyst keeps (`poc/seeds/`); keys are written by code so an article-born candidate for the same quantity merges into the seed (D190 exact-key identity) and the placer's 'takes' line is the one every keyed question gets. The template routes and never gates (D208): extraction and candidate opening are unchanged. Ladders of the four seeds that the control run also opened are copied from that run; the new ones are drafts marked as such for the analyst to confirm.\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md-3003-- Measured next (three draws against three control draws, the same 14 days, end to end): core and supporting matters reaching judgement and dropped for no home, noise reaching judgement, questions opened and their duplicates. The driver-in-force block for the judge and re-placement of earlier statements (D208's later steps) are not built here.\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md-3004-\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md-3005-## D254 · 2026-11-01 · Placement: a question's code-written 'takes' line is the one rule for its file; D207's \"company-wide figure questions take only their own figures\" is retired\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md-3006-\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md-3007-- Alex, when the two placement calls were put to him as questions (2026-11-01 night): \"你自己回答自己好吗这种傻逼问题你有这么多context和prd 以及人设，你为什么不自己回答\". Decided by Claude under that delegation, from the signed standard, the decisions and the analyst persona; recorded here so the departure from D207 is written before any default moves.\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md-3008-- The mechanism (`research/2026-11-01-e2e-loop/plan.md` §3.2′): one placement request, read as the model reads it, held two rulebooks. The system prompt (`placement-narrow-v2`, D207's wording) said a company-wide figure question \"takes only the company's own reported figures, guidance, estimates of that figure and management's statements about it\"; the code-written takes line of the same question said \"figures, guidance, estimates and revisions for <scope> over <period>, and the direct drivers of that figure stated with a size\". The model followed the system prompt: SemiAnalysis's estimate of data-center revenue 3/3 filed under none with the data-center question open, Morgan Stanley's rack price the same, a hyperscaler's own capex guidance 3/3 under none against the hyperscaler-capex question. The system prompt also called filing under none \"a valid answer, not a failure\", and the placer filed 74% of extracted statements nowhere, two fifths of them gold-kept.\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md-3009-- Decided: the takes line is the one rule for what a question's file holds; the system prompt (`placement-narrow-v4`, 1,311 characters against v2's 1,587) says only how to apply it: narrowest covering question, that one only; a covered statement belongs in the file whoever says it (the company, a named analyst or bank, a customer, a competitor, a reporter) and with or without a period, basis or exact amount, the weight being the judge's; the period in a takes line tells questions apart and bars no driver from another period when no open question covers it; nothing a takes line covers is filed under none. D207's \"only their own\" sentence goes: an analyst betting on a company's revenue reads every credible estimate of it, and the signed standard keeps third-party estimates as core (gold v5: SemiAnalysis, Morgan Stanley). The anti-sink gate D207 wanted is the takes line's own \"direct drivers of that figure stated with a size\" plus the narrowest-question rule and the driver questions (D253 seeds); the 2026-10-31 stored re-send showed that removing the \"only their own\" sentence filed 11 more gold homes and no more noise. The event takes line (`placement.takes()`) now also names \"cancellations, design or configuration changes\", the content of a v2 sentence the proof showed the takes line lacked (a scrapped alternative rack plan 2/3 → 0/3 without it); the catch-all measure `other` is no longer printed as a word.\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md-3010-- Measured before the send ($0, `resend_place_set.py`, stored requests re-sent three times as stored and three times changed, `proof-v4-final.txt`): of 17 core statements of matters that reached no question, filed in at least two of three sends 3 → 8; supporting 1 → 4 of 5; the 12 gold not-kept guards 0 → 0. A reviewer-driven weakening of two sentences (`proof-v4-final-b.txt`) lost the effect (core 3 → 3): the proven text is the one kept. Arm 3 (three draws, `poc-v86`) measures it end to end against the seed-v2 arm; the sink guard is the links a draw puts on the total and segment revenue questions (r1: 66/72/76 of 335/374/370). The default configuration stays `poc-v69` until the arm is read; a switch is a separate record.\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md-3011-\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md-3012-## D255 · 2026-11-01 · The extraction's one-line summary names the matter the statement belongs to (the next arm after D254's)\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md-3013-\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md-3014-- Alex, the same words as D254 (the question was put to him as `plan.md` §5 (f)). Decided by Claude under that delegation.\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md-3015-- The class (`research/2026-11-01-e2e-loop/dropped-census-r2-placement-v3.md`): of the 25 gold core matters the seed-v2 arms dropped at placement, 11 had their question open; 6–7 of those 11 are one story, the Rubin Ultra rack delay of 2026-07-05/06, whose statements say \"NVL72x2\", \"two Oberon racks back to back\", \"a backup plan bolting two racks together\", \"our roadmap is intact\", while the question says \"Rubin Ultra / Kyber NVL144\". The placer reads the item's title line, the statements (one-line summary and quote) and the open questions, never the article (D207); it cannot connect a statement to a matter the statement does not name. The company's own denial in the same article, which names the roadmap, was filed. No placement wording can fix this class: three proofs filed 0 of 3 of these statements under every variant.\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md-3016-- Decided: the one-line summary stands alone, as an analyst's note card does: who, what, how much, and the matter the statement belongs to, by the name the article uses (a product generation, a deal, a process, a market) when the statement itself uses another name or a part's name. The rule is written where the field is defined today: the role prompt's one sentence on `one_line` (role-v53 line 16: \"a standalone summary … who did or said what, how much and for which period, naming the measure even when a neighbouring sentence gives it\") gains \"and the matter it belongs to\"; the schema's `one_line` carries no description, and moving the definition there is the same change in another place (AGENTS §7.3), decided when the arm is written. General words that read the same for any company; no list of names, no company's products. It is built after arm 3 is read (no edit to package code while a run is live) and measured as an extraction change: the whole bench, three draws against the stored v53 draws (field correctness read by hand on the dropped class and on a sample of unchanged statements), then the end-to-end funnel.\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md-3017-\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md-3018-## D256 · 2026-11-01 · D255's sentence refuted by its proof; the mechanism is the undefined `links` field. One decider with the article, the open questions and one code-written rule is a PROPOSAL for Alex, not a decision\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md-3019-\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md-3020-- The one-line-summary sentence D255 prescribed was re-sent on the four rack-delay articles' stored extraction requests (`research/2026-11-01-e2e-loop/proof-d255-oneline.txt`, three sends as stored, three with the sentence): the summaries did not change (NVL72x2 and the backup plan are still named only as themselves). Per AGENTS §1 a fix that does not flip its case is not built; `role-v53b.txt` stays byte-identical to `role-v53.txt`.\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md-3021-- The model's own account, two cases (`probe-d255-links.txt`): it left the backup-plan and NVL72x2 statements unlinked from its own Kyber candidate because it read `links` as \"evidence that settles the candidate\" (\"One thesis concerns one figure or one event\"), and it agrees, reading the article, that both belong to the Kyber matter. The request defines `links` nowhere: the schema field has no description and the only sentence about it says which ids to use. A field without a definition is a coin flip per send (AGENTS §6).\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md-3022-- Proposed, not decided (an architecture change was left to Alex on 2026-10-31 and stays his; recording this as decided on the night of 2026-11-01 was an overreach, corrected after his 23:45 message \"你在给我新架构之前有没有想过自己在耍什么智障一直跑一些没用的东西\"; the review is `research/2026-11-01-e2e-loop/review-2026-11-02.md`): the structural cause of the whole class is that one analyst's judgement, \"this statement bears on this bet\", is split across three calls that each hold half the information (extraction has the article and no questions; placement has the questions, a summary and 240 characters of quote; matching only questions). The fix is one decider with the whole article, the day's open questions with their code-written takes lines, and the `links` field defined by that same rule (owner: `placement.takes`'s clauses). It would be extraction version 72 (role-v53's text, the day's open questions shown with takes lines, the links definition in the schema, no separate placement call), one of three ways to give the filing judgement its information (the review §4 lists them with a lean); nothing of it is built or applied until Alex chooses. The 2026-10-31 arm of the same shape (v82, `design-v71-production.md`) failed on two wirings this version does not repeat: its role text halved the candidates (\"only for a matter no open question covers\") and its links bypassed the filing rule.\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md-3023-\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md-3024-## D257 · 2026-11-01 · A declaration that is a stored group under other names gives the group those names (D166, the alias half); question identity R2 applied\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md-3025-\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md-3026-- Census on one 14-day draw (`e2e-loop/plan.md` §3.8): of 35 declared groups that folded into a stored group by a shared name, 23 carried names the stored group lacked; the Kyber rack group never learnt NVL72x2, Oberon or NVL144 although three articles declared them, so the placer's takes line never showed them and the statements using those names were dropped in every draw.\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md-3027-- Decided (same delegation): `groups.plan` returns the declared names a stored group lacks and the writer appends them (`thesis_group_aliases`, append-only; `store.add_group_aliases`); every reader of a group's aliases (the placer's takes line, membership by alias, group search) sees the creation's names plus the added ones; the takes line prints every name, not the first six. D166's rule for what an alias may be is unchanged (products, projects, programmes, parties; never a research object's name). Test `tests/test_group_alias_merge.py`; `test_groups.py`'s expectation of the SK Telecom case follows this decision (the deployment's names join the Rubin group).\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:3028:- The question-identity rules of D248 items 2–3 (R2-a: an open event question takes the same event under another deadline; R2-b: a generation's launch and shipment are one question), built on 2026-10-31 on branch `fix/question-identity-r2` and accepted at $0 by replaying the stored matching decisions (55 blind-judged duplicates: 22 merged, 0 false merges), are applied to the working tree (no commit, at Alex's word) and measured with the alias change as one identity arm (`log.md` row 4), control = arm 3.\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md-3029-\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:3030:## D258 · 2026-11-02 · Question identity brought in line with D248: a part of an open question is filed under it; `event` and `policy_event` are one family and a process's step words are one process; the collision judge is given D248's test\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md-3031-\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md-3032-- Alex, 2026-11-02 00:05, on why questions were duplicated although the matching step sees every open question: \"开题为什么重复？你不是都可以看到存在的题了吗那你操他妈的在干嘛你到底系统有没有接对\"; then \"我刚才说的这个问题你也发现是什么 part of 问题你不该去反思一下这个设计或是哪里有问题直接修直接改。开干。用这个思路来一个一个的提升我们的能力。不要陷入无限没必要的测试循环\".\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:3033:- The wiring is as designed (every candidate is compared with every open question by Jev, and the collision judge is asked); the duplicates come from the identity rules, which predate D248. Census of the 23 questions one draw's articles opened (arm 3 d1, `research/2026-11-01-e2e-loop/review-2026-11-02.md`; the three draws in `replay-part-of-r3.txt`): 10 were ones Jev had called `part_of` an open question (ZTE's H200 licence of the China authorization question, the CoreWeave backstop and the credit-support programme of the financing-commitments total, Rubin shipping by September of Rubin launching by December), and `part_of` fell through to \"new question\"; 5 were deadline variants or a launch beside a shipment (R2-a/b, built 2026-10-31, measured only tonight as arm 4); 1 opened because the model typed the China H200 authorization as `event` against the seed's `policy_event` and two more because its event-type word for the one licensing process varied (licence, approval, other), each a typed-field conflict that blocked a Jev \"same\" of 0.85–0.92 before the judge was ever asked; 3 are the GAAP/non-GAAP and growth/level variants (R2-d, open); 4 were new matters.\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:3034:- Decided (under D248's general rule, \"two questions are one when the same outcome settles both; they are kept apart only when their answers can move apart and an analyst would bet on each separately\", its item 1 \"a single deal under a plan already opened by amount merges into it\" and item 6 \"a small part opens no question\"):\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:3035:  - R2-e: a candidate Jev calls `part_of` an open question (above the threshold) is filed under that question, like a `same_quantity_or_event` verdict, when the typed fields allow; the part is evidence of the card, not a card of its own. The typed fields still decide: a yes/no signing question never merges into an amount question (D248 item 1's recorded exception, the Ohio lease guarantee) because `event` and `financing_amount` conflict. The collision judge is consulted as before and may keep a component apart under its rule.\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md-3036-  - R2-f: in `identity.conflicts`, `event` and `policy_event` are one measure family, and for a policy process the event-type word is not identity (a licence, an approval and an unnamed step of one process are one process); a product event's type still distinguishes a deployment from the generation's launch and shipment (R2-b).\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:3037:  - The collision judge's prompt gains D248's test (`collision-v2.txt`): a single deal, counterparty or instance under a plan or process already asked about, and a step or deadline of one event, are the same question; a component is a question of its own only when its scale alone can change revenue, profit, cash or credit risk and an analyst watches it separately. Proof on the 50 stored judge requests of arm 3 d1, two sends each with the stored prompt and two with v2 (`proof-collision-v2.txt`): of 113 \"distinct question, same matter\" verdicts, 28 became a merge verdict (same question 17, same question other period 11) and 36 became \"different\" (the same outcome for the code, no merge); of 66 \"same question\" verdicts 2 moved to \"distinct\"; the credit-support programme, the GPU rental commitments, the AI-cloud credit support and the Rubin platform launch flipped in both sends, the GAAP margin, the memory share and the supply commitments stayed apart.\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md-3038-- $0 acceptance (`harness/replay_part_of.py`, the stored Jev verdicts and keys of arm 3's three draws replayed through the new rules): of 23 / 26 / 25 questions the articles opened, 10 / 13 / 15 merge into the open question an analyst would hold (the financing total, the China authorization, the Kyber and Rubin questions, the non-GAAP margin, the Vera CPU revenue), 1 of the 38 is questionable (supply commitments filed under the CoreWeave capacity purchase, Jev `part_of` 0.57), and the Ohio signing question stays apart in every draw. Still open after this decision: the near-threshold Jev verdicts on launch-vs-shipment pairs whose scopes carry different names (Kyber vs Rubin Ultra, 0.35–0.48: the names belong to one research group, R2-g), and the GAAP/non-GAAP and growth/level variants (R2-d).\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md-3039-- Tests: `tests/test_identity_part_of.py`; `test_collision_judge.py`'s case \"without a collision setting Jev decides alone\" now expects the merge (the spec changed here, recorded before the test). Measured by replay, not by a paid arm (Alex: \"不要再跑这些有的没的臂了\"); the configuration that names `collision-v2` is `poc-v89` (poc-v86 otherwise); the default stays `poc-v69`.\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md-3040-\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md-3041-## D259 · 2026-11-02 · The takes line takes the evidence that bears on a question's answer, not only its own figures: D254's \"direct drivers stated with a size\" gate goes; supporting evidence gets its leeway\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md-3042-\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md-3043-- Alex, 2026-11-02 morning, asked what to do with the supporting evidence the standard keeps but no question takes (74 gold supporting matters a draw dropped at placement, 88% with no bet under the library and the takes lines; the three options put to him were drop and tighten the standard, a company file outside the judgement, or widen the takes line at the cost of the revenue sinks): \"先放款take 吧，辅助反正就是个中间地带我们给点leeway\".\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md-3044-- Mechanism (arm 3's 51 supporting matters dropped in every draw read one by one, `research/2026-11-01-e2e-loop/supporting-dropped-read-r3.txt`; one placement request read as the model reads it, `review-2026-11-02.md` §7): the figure question's takes line ended \"and the direct drivers of that figure stated with a size\", and the event and policy lines named only the event's own steps. The size gate contradicted the same request's system prompt (\"even when it gives no period, basis or exact amount\") and D240, and \"direct drivers\" excluded what the standard files as supporting: another company's operating figures (§6), a named customer's, supplier's or competitor's action (§5.1 item 2), anything reached through D250 item 2's path test. Half the dropped class is named partner, customer and competitor actions without an amount (Palantir's Nemotron integration, DeepSeek's chip, SambaNova's round, JPMorgan choosing SambaNova), a fifth is other companies' numbers (Broadcom's AI revenue guide, Micron's margin, Google Cloud's backlog), the rest demand and supply colour with an open home (the NVL576 delay and the Oberon stopgap of the Kyber question, TSMC's fabs, the AI debt market of the backstop questions), enforcement details of the H200 process, and consensus or valuation figures.\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md-3045-- Decided (code, `placement.takes()`, under every configuration): a figure question's file takes its figures, guidance, estimates and revisions \"and what makes that figure more or less likely: the demand, supply, competition and pricing behind it\" (the standard's 5.1 test and D250 item 2's four paths); a launch, shipment or deployment event's file also takes the event's \"variants and stopgaps\"; a deal or obligation's file also takes \"the counterparties' own plans, financing and demand that bear on it\"; a policy process's file also takes \"its enforcement and evasion … and the affected parties' own plans and statements about it\". The system prompt `placement-narrow-v4` is unchanged: it says how the line is applied (whoever says it, with or without a size, the narrowest covering question only, nothing a line covers is filed under none). The weight stays the judge's. The sink D207 guarded against is accepted as the price of the leeway, bounded by the narrowest-question rule and the driver questions.\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md-3046-- Proof (`proof-takes-wide.txt`; `harness/resend_takes_wide.py`: every stored placement request of arm 4 draw 1, 212 requests, re-sent once with the four clauses edited in the stored text, the edit checked byte for byte against the code on the run's 46 questions; one draw, one send, $0.18 at list price): gold supporting matters with a filed statement 40 → 98 of the extracted ones, core 69 → 75; statements filed 358 → 690 and links 390 → 717 over the draw; links on the total and Data Center revenue questions 22% → 32% of all links (Data Center 48 → 152, total revenue 39 → 79, the accelerator-share question 8 → 78, China share 17 → 38). By gold class over the 104 gold-article requests: supporting statements gaining a home 62, losing 0; core 11 and 2; gold not-kept 41 and 1; unlisted 23 and 1; optional 12 and 0. The two core losses were sampler noise: sent three times as stored and three times changed, the company's \"nearly $20 billion in CPU sales\" statement is filed 1/3 → 3/3 under the Vera CPU question and the \"80% of core technologies domestic\" statement 2/3 → 3/3 under the China share question (`proof-takes-wide-lost-core.txt`). The first wording also named \"decisions behind it\", a word D250 does not have: it filed hires, an R&D centre, game launches and an executive's pay under revenue and margin questions (`proof-takes-wide-a-with-decisions.txt`: not-kept gains 53, unlisted 35, total revenue 39 → 115, sink share 36%); the word was removed and the proof re-run (the numbers above), the supporting class unchanged (97 → 98).\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md-3047-- What the leeway costs, written down: the noise the placement step used to remove is the extraction's noise and now reaches the judge (41 gold not-kept statements over the gold articles of one draw: ecosystem adoption lists, a CEO's generic claim, restated known deals, one game expansion under total revenue). The share of noise among pieces reaching judgement, 15% in arm 4, is estimated at about 22% after this change (from the gold-article counts, not measured end to end); filed statements double, so the judgement count and cost a draw are estimated to grow by 60–90% (arm 4: 310 judgements, $0.92 a draw; judging-v6's longer answers add to it). The owner of that noise is the extraction standard's 5.1 item 5 and 5.3 (common knowledge, current arrangements, product details), not the placement step; it is the next class to count, at the extraction. Tests: `tests/test_placement.py` (the D259 case). Measured by re-sent stored requests, not by an arm (Alex: \"不要再跑这些有的没的臂了\"); the default configuration stays `poc-v69`, and since the change is code every configuration run from now on carries it.\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md-3048-\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md-3049-## D260 · 2026-11-02 · A judgement is a forecast against a reference: the rung the evidence in force makes most likely, judged against what the market expects; the answer states the reference and the implied outcome (judging-v6)\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md-3050-\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md-3051-- Alex, 2026-11-02, asked whether the judge's stance should stay an absolute-band lookup (the current reading) or be judged relative to expectations: \"门槛没有标准，按照你作为 hedge fund analyst 的认识来定\". Decided by Claude under that delegation: the definition below is Claude's analyst judgement, recorded as such, not Alex's words.\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md-3052-- Mechanism (arm 4 draw 1, all 356 judgements read, `research/2026-11-01-e2e-loop/review-2026-11-02.md` §7 and `proof-judging-v6.txt`): 8 of 314 later judgements moved a rung and 320 of 356 reasons say \"remains\"; the FY2027 total revenue question was judged 12 times at neutral while its upward pushes grew from 1 to 35, every reason \"the $392 billion estimate is inside the band … does not establish $400 billion\"; the gross-margin judgement wrote \"leans toward rung 2 but does not warrant moving\"; the 2027 hyperscaler-capex theme stayed below the band management's own forecast names because the forecast \"is not fact\". The judging-v5 prompt asked the judge to \"be precise about what is established\" and said only fact can establish a rung: the model read \"established\" as the bar for leaving a rung and the consensus figure as the anchor. A second cause stays open: the ladder's neutral band is written at opening without naming what it compares against (PRD 06 ladder rule 2 asks for it); that is the extraction's rule and is not changed here.\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md-3053-- Decided, the analyst's rule: (1) the rung is a forecast, the outcome the evidence in force makes most likely at the due date, not the one it has proved; \"not established\" is a statement of confidence, never a reason to stay. (2) The reference is what the market expects: consensus, the company's guidance, the stated plan or deadline; a consensus or guidance figure alone keeps the judgement at the reference's rung and, once other evidence has arrived, is never the reason to stay. (3) The judge derives the outcome the evidence implies (reported figures and guidance give a run-rate; a quantified revision, a customer's demand number, a supplier's constraint, a confirmed delay or cancellation shift it), checks it against the dependencies' conclusions (a part cannot exceed its whole; a figure spanning several periods or products gives the question only its share), compares it with the rung boundaries and moves when it crosses one. (4) Weight follows tier and novelty: fact fixes what is known; party statements are the strongest forecast input; third-party views and rumours move the forecast in proportion to their specificity; a repeat, another outlet or an opinion with no new fact or calculation moves nothing. (5) The answer states `reference` and `implied_outcome` as required fields from `judging-v6` (`judging.schema_for`; code refuses an empty one; stored beside the rung in `judgements.reference` / `implied_outcome`; a ledger written before v6 gains the columns at its first write), so the D3 stance gold can read the reasoning, not only the rung. Written where the judgement is specified: PRD 06 State rules (`docs/system-design/new-facts.js` STATE_RULES, the generated block) and this record.\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md-3054-- Proof (`proof-judging-v6.txt`, `proof-judging-v6b.txt`: the last stored judgement request of 14 theses of arm 4 draw 1 re-sent once each under v6 and read beside the stored v5 answers, about a cent): every answer names the reference and derives the implied outcome. Six rungs moved against the stored ones: non-GAAP gross margin 3 → 2 (Q1 reported 75% and Q2 guided 75% sit on the rung-2 boundary), 2027 hyperscaler capex 4 → 5 (management's own \"more than $1 trillion\"), China accelerator share 4 → 5 (share \"fallen to zero\"), China H200 authorization No → Yes (a reported plan to permit named firms and reported progress in reviews, six months before the deadline), Data Center revenue 2 → 3 ($355–360 billion derived from Q1 and the total-revenue proxy, below the $360 billion boundary), Blackwell+Rubin revenue 2 → 1 in the first send by annualising a two-year \"$1 trillion visibility\" figure to $545 billion, a part above its whole: clause (3)'s consistency check was added for it and the re-send gives rung 2 ($320–360 billion, a share of the Data Center segment). Total revenue stays at 3 with the arithmetic shown (H1 $172.6 billion from Q1 and the Q2 guide; $400 billion needs more than $227 billion in H2). Prompt 2,453 → 3,782 characters: the request defined neither what a rung means nor a reference and its \"established\" wording forced the defect; the two sentences that carried it were cut. Configuration `poc-v90` (poc-v89 with judging-v6); the default stays `poc-v69`. Tests: `tests/test_stance_fields.py`. Measured by re-sent stored requests, not by an arm (Alex: \"不要再跑这些有的没的臂了\").\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md-3055-\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md-3056-## D261 · 2026-11-02 · A ruler or gold that is built and reviewed is never changed again\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md-3057-\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md-3058-- Alex, 2026-11-02, while the judgement ruler (D3) was being built: \"你的尺子做出来和金标真的不能再动了，已经造成了3天的各种漂移，非常的严重，我需要你记录到我们的决策和原则里面，我们做完的review过的尺子金标不能再动了\".\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:3059:- The drift he names, counted: the extraction ruler went from the first standard (D229, 2026-10-29) to the signed page version 3 (D243, the same day) to version 5 (D250, 2026-10-31), the gold was re-derived from version 3 to version 5 with 62 recorded changes, and every score between D248 and 2026-10-31 had been read against the version-3 gold (the \"假的测量\" of 2026-10-31); the judgement step had no ruler at all until today. Three days of numbers that cannot be compared with each other.\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md-3060-- Decided (his words; written at the decision it governs, AGENTS §7.1): once a ruler and its gold have been reviewed (readers who did not write them read them against the decisions; Alex signed), neither the definition nor the gold changes again. A defect found later is a dated correction record beside the gold (`corrections-*.json`), printed with every score and never merged in. A new definition is a new version that only his decision opens, with its own gold derived from scratch; old scores stay as they were and are never compared with the new. A ruler under construction is edited only until that review, and nothing is scored against it before.\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md-3061-- What is locked by this record: the extraction standard page (`docs/prd/05-extraction-standard.html`, version 3 signed D243, with D250's four boundaries and counting unit) and `golden-v5/` (sha256 in `golden-v5.sha256`): no version 6; the loop's desk ruler (`research/2026-11-01-e2e-loop/README.md`, D1–D3). What is still under construction and locks at his review: the judgement ruler `research/2026-11-01-e2e-loop/judgement-gold/ruler-v1.md`, its reader brief, question list and gold `gold-v1.json` (the sign-off is a separate record).\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md-3062-\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md-3063-## D262 · 2026-11-02 · The judgement ruler (D3) and its gold are fixed: the gold is reader B's answers; frozen at sha256 636c056d1e4252fa…\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md-3064-\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md-3065-- Alex, 2026-11-02, after reading the two readers' reasoning on every disagreement (readers A and B differed on 3 of 23 questions by range or yes/no and on 12 of 20 direction labels; the system disagreed with the draft on the total revenue and Vera CPU questions in every draw): \"那就不要理A了；我们就go with B 好吧，定下尺子金表\".\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md-3066-- Fixed by that decision: the ruler `research/2026-11-01-e2e-loop/judgement-gold/ruler-v1.md` (unit: a gold question at the window end 2026-07-14; material: golden-v5's 309 items by sha; a numeric question agrees when the gold's implied range overlaps the band of the rung the judge chose, a yes/no question when the answers match; the two null baselines printed with every score); the question list and the must_open mapping as built (`questions-v1.json`, 22 seeds + the Ohio guarantee); the gold `gold-v1.json` = reader B's 23 answers verbatim (B: a fresh-context Claude reader, model-authored, 3 questions marked no material: CoWoS capacity, semiconductor growth, SK Telecom), sha256 `636c056d1e4252fa759660803067e6ccd67a81067b012905e918aa9dec4005f2` in `gold-v1.sha256` and in `score_judgement.py`, which refuses any other. Reader A (Codex) stays beside it as the control record (`reader-A.json`, `reconcile-v1.md`): its distance from B is the stick's own noise. Claude's two proposals of the afternoon (a three-level score when readers split; toss-up questions excluded) were not adopted: one range per question, every question counts. From here D261 applies: nothing in the ruler or the gold changes; a defect is a dated record in `corrections-v1.json`.\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md-3067-- First measurement on the frozen gold (`score-r4-identity.txt`, arm 4, three draws, judging-v5): judged questions agreeing 13/19, 15/18, 12/17; the lookup baseline (the rung containing the gold's reference figure) 9/15, 8/14, 8/14; always-neutral 5/11, 5/10, 5/10. Disagreeing in every draw: FY2027 total revenue (gold $400–435 billion, judge neutral by consensus lookup) and Vera CPU revenue (gold $8–18 billion, judge the top rung on management's $20 billion at face value); in two of three: the financing-commitments total (gold $25–60 billion, judge $10–20 billion). Never judged in any draw: NVIDIA's own capex (q12); the operating margin in two draws (q10): evidence never reached them, counted apart as \"no judgement\". The new judge (`judging-v6`, D260) has no run to score yet; a run on `poc-v90` is Alex's call.\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md-3068-\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md-3069-## D263 · 2026-11-02 · The judge is written to the frozen gold's own reasoning (judging-v7, poc-v91); a gap to the gold is closed in the judge, not re-measured\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md-3070-\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md-3071-- Alex, after the first score on the frozen gold was reported as the system being \"wrong\" on some questions: \"不是啊什么叫错？我不是和你说了就按照claude的标准来就好了嘛\". The gold is Claude's (reader B's) standard by D262; a disagreement is the distance between the judge and that standard, to be closed in the judge's rule, not a verdict to be measured again.\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md-3072-- What reader B does that judging-v6 did not, read from B's answers on the questions that differed (`judgement-gold/reconcile-v1.md`, `gold-v1.json`): carries the guided growth forward rather than annualising the last quarter flat (Data Center, total revenue); discounts a management target for a product with no shipments by default (Vera CPU: two selling quarters, four million units at $5,000, the company's own choice of another CPU); sizes an announced but unsized commitment from its disclosed comparable (the Firmus backstop from Sharon's); derives a figure no one states from the accounting identities in the evidence (capex from operating less free cash flow); keeps linked conclusions consistent (China share against the H200 authorization theme). Written into `judging-v7.txt` as five clauses (v6 3,782 → 4,924 characters; reason: each clause is a behaviour of the frozen standard the judge lacked), named by `poc-v91`; schema and code unchanged.\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md-3073-- Proof on the stored requests of the questions whose arm-4 judgement differed from the gold (`proof-judging-v7a.txt`, `proof-judging-v7.txt`; one send each, cents): total revenue rung 3 → 2 (about $421 billion from the guided growth on FY2026's base; gold $400–435 billion), Data Center 3 → 2 (about $372 billion; gold $370–400 billion), Vera CPU 1 → 2 ($12 to below $20 billion, the target discounted for the volume not in hand; gold $8–18 billion), DRAM prices 3 → 2 (about +15%; gold +10–35%), financing total stays 4 ($33.5–39.8 billion; gold $25–60 billion), the Ohio guarantee stays Yes; China share stays below 1% in draw 1, consistent with that draw's H200 theme judged No (the gold has the authorization likely and the share 1–8%; the consistency clause ties the share to the theme, so it moves with it). Six of the seven re-sent questions now land in the gold's band; the end-to-end agreement under judging-v7 needs a run on `poc-v91`, which is Alex's call. A placement gap seen on the way: the Vera CPU question never held the fall-launch statement (filed under the Rubin launch questions), so the judge could not count selling quarters from evidence; the default-discount clause covers it, the filing is a D2 class to count.\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md-3074-\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md-3075-## D264 · 2026-11-02 · The extraction reads the day's open questions with their takes lines and files the statements itself (extraction v72, poc-v92): the one-decider architecture Alex chose is built and measured against poc-v91 on the frozen ruler\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md-3076-\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md-3077-- Alex, 2026-11-02 evening, after asking why the open library was never adopted as the extraction's context (\"你为什么架构上没有采纳我说的开的库作为step 2 context\"; the answer traced the chain from his 10-31 instruction through the one-draw v82 replay I judged \"不采用\" myself to the D256 proposal left waiting): \"我们非常专注的验证这个架构选择：我们有金标和尺子frozen可以比；我们这个架构设计的核心就是透过适当的Prompt 和引入已经开的题，和题的叙述来决定抽取；现在最新的prompt有修改了很多小毛病，你看是不是用最新最好的prompt + v72这边告诉模型怎么用读取开题库的prompt 来做新的实验prompt。充分理解我的ask然后get it worked out\". This is his choice of the one-decider architecture (review-2026-11-02.md §4 way (i), the D256 proposal) and of its base prompt.\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md-3078-- Built (design: `research/2026-11-01-e2e-loop/design-v72.md`, the four tables of AGENTS §2, predictions frozen at sha256 `aec1bb40…` in `predictions-v72.sha256` before any send): extraction version 72, named by `poc/config/poc-v92.json` (= poc-v91 with T*-v72 and no placement setting). The request shows the questions open at the start of the item's day (D251's snapshot) each with the code-written takes line the placer read (`placement.question_lines`, one writer for both requests); the schema defines the evidence field `links` by the same rule (`placement.FILING_RULE`, the placer's v4 system-prompt rule restated beside the field: the narrowest open question whose takes line covers the statement, whoever says it, with or without a period or amount, plus the answer's own candidates, else empty); `role-v72.txt` is `role-v66.txt` with its first paragraph pointing at [Open questions] and the links field (the latest extraction prompt on the frozen extraction gold: v53 → v65 gold-rejected kept per draw about 109 → 59 with core and supporting flat, v66 = v65 + R3's boundary, `r3-final-scores-Y6.txt`); `categories-v72.json` and `review-v72.txt` are v66's. The extraction's links file each statement: one linked to an open question is filed there, one linked only to its candidates follows them, one linked to nothing is dropped as 'no home' (D209; the handover's reason is the same word, so `e2e_funnel` and `dropped_census` read it); no placement call exists for v72 (`extraction.one_decider`, `places` ends at v71). v71's `new_in_it` and `moves` fields are not asked (`MOVES_FIELDS_VERSIONS`). Settled by me under the delegation of 2026-11-01, and said so: the candidate rules stay v66's (propose when the item raises it; code owns identity and folds a duplicate of an open question, D258), not v71's \"only for a matter no open question covers\", which halved the candidates and the homes in v82; it is one sentence to tighten if the questions ruler says so.\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md-3079-- Two wirings of D251's snapshot were wrong and are fixed in the same change, each with a test that fails on its mutant (`tests/test_one_decider.py`): (1) before the first completed day the snapshot was empty, so the seeds (seq 0, D253) were invisible to every first-day item while the placer of poc-v91 saw them (`store.day_start_seq` is 0 before the first completed day); (2) the takes line prints a question's group names and aliases, which D257's alias merges change within a day, so the request bytes would have changed mid-day, the parallel day would have re-sent every waiting request, and two items of one day would have seen different lists (`store.groups_of_view_at` reads memberships and aliases at the snapshot's seq). Version gates: v53's and v71's request bytes are unchanged (tests); 274 tests pass; `scripts/preflight.py` over arm 4 draw 1 replays 243 stored answers through the current checks with the same 22 refusals as before (`preflight-v72-prep.txt`).\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md-3080-- Proof before the run (cents; `harness/resend_extract_v72.py`, `proof-v72-links.txt`: the four rack-delay articles of 2026-07-05/06 rebuilt under v72 from arm 4 draw 1's day-start snapshots, three sends each; the stored outcome of the same run as the control). The statements that name nothing (\"Our roadmap is intact\", the scrapped backup plan, NVL72x2 back-to-back racks), which the placer dropped or filed under same-day duplicate questions in every arm since 10-31, are filed under the seed question v18 (Rubin Ultra / Kyber NVL144 shipping) in 3/3 sends of the SemiAnalysis article (both statements), 3/3 of the Tom's Hardware article (NVL72x2; the denial 2/3 with one send's quote refused), 3/3 of the Cramer article (to v18, v2 or v31 by send), while in the Asian-suppliers article the NVL72x2 statement went once to no home and twice to the revenue questions (v1/v2, v2/v20: a sink link; the Kyber question v33 the control's placer used was opened that same day and is outside the snapshot). Zero candidates in 27 sends over nine matched articles against the control's four, all four Kyber duplicates of v18 (the list shown does the deduplication the matching step did after the fact). Request size 22–38K characters (27–44 open questions) against the control's mean 19.8K.\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md-3081-- The measurement, launched 2026-11-02 18:05 at his \"get it worked out\": `arms/r6-one-decider-v92/d1..3` against `arms/r6-control-v91/d1..3` (the acceptance run he stopped at 17:27, now the control, since arm 4 and v92 are separated by D258, D259 and D263 as well), 2026-07-01..14, seeds v2, eight extraction workers each, cap $3 a draw; scored on the frozen ruler (`e2e_funnel.py`, `score_judgement.py`), regressions first, every number, in `log.md` row 12 and `design-v72.md` §8. Whether poc-v92 becomes the default is his call after the numbers.\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md-3082-- Measured (six draws finished 19:40; `e2e-funnel-r6-v72.txt`, `judgement-gold/score-r6-*`, `matter-states-r6-v72.txt`, `probe-v72-sink.txt`; three-draw means, v91 → v92). Regressions first: core matters reaching judgement 76.3 → 73.7 of 86 (predicted ≥ +2, the null is ±2), core dropped for no home 4.0 → 5.7, article-opened questions 11.7 → 3.0 (candidates 65 → 6.7: the list shown suppresses proposals even with the candidate rule unchanged; must_open 28/28 and may_open 40/42 in both arms because the seeds cover them, the Ohio guarantee being the one visible loss), supporting not extracted 25.3 → 46.0. Held: supporting reaching 94.0 → 90.0 (at the −4 line), noise reaching 89.2 → 56.9 (−36%), judgement agreement 17/19, 17/18, 17/19 → 15/18, 16/17, 17/18 against lookup 8–9/14–15, cost $1.15 → $0.88 a draw with model time −36% and wall clock 95 → 46 minutes for three draws, zero re-sent requests. Two mechanisms, both in sentences and neither in the architecture: (1) the sink is back: 60–62% of links on the three company-wide revenue questions against v91's 34–40%, 190–208 statements a draw under both total and Data Center revenue against 5–6; the model's own account in three of three cases cites the figure-line takes clause D259 added (\"what makes that figure more or less likely: the demand, supply, competition and pricing behind it\") and concedes the links field's \"narrowest only\" should have excluded the broader question or the link altogether; (2) role-v66's end-of-request check removes 21 supporting matters a draw that v53 keeps (20 matters extracted in v91 in at least two draws and in v92 in at most one: third parties' actions and views, named hires and partners, product milestones, standard §5.1 kinds 2–3), a loss the extraction bench's \"supporting in at least two draws\" count had hidden. Verdict: as built, v72 is neither better nor worse than v91 on the desk's counts and is cleaner, cheaper and faster; it does not become the default and no further arm is sent before the two mechanisms are fixed at their owners with $0 proofs: the root/driver pair collapsed to the narrower question by code (identity, D207's rule), the figure-line clause reworded and proved on re-sent stored v92 requests, and the base text (v53 against v66 under the architecture) put to Alex.\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md-3083-\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md-3084-## D265 · 2026-11-02 · Extraction v72 / poc-v92 is the version: the default configuration, the base every later change builds on, the control of every later measurement; D207's narrowest rule is enforced in code\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md-3085-\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md-3086-- Alex, 2026-11-02 evening, on the measured v72: \"for the current version that you just fixed, I think it's highly probable that it's going to be the candidate. So, clean up the versioning. Like, whatever we just did, I think this is going to be the latest version. Use this, and don't drift again. With that, start to experiment the next steps that you talked about on what you need to do to fix the problems that you have discovered that still could be enhanced.\" The base-text question of D264 (v53 against v66) is thereby answered: the version is v72 as measured (role-v66's text under the architecture); its supporting-recall loss is fixed inside it, not by reverting its base.\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md-3087-- Versioning from here: `poc/config/poc-v92.json` is the default (`scripts/replay.py`, the default-entry test `test_replay_script_defaults_run_the_default_jev_configuration_with_sixteen_and_eight_workers`, the README name it; `poc-v69` stays as the record of the placement architecture). A change to an extraction text is a new number (v73, v74 …: its own role, categories and review files, byte-identical where the text is unchanged) and a new `poc` configuration built from v92; a code rule applies under every configuration and changes no number. Every later measurement names poc-v92 as its control, three draws each, on the frozen ruler (§7.1); the 2026-11-02 draws `arms/r6-one-decider-v92/d1..3` are its baseline (`e2e-funnel-r6-v72.txt`). Nothing of the request shape (the day-start snapshot with takes lines, the links definition, no placement call) changes again without a decision in his words.\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md-3088-- The first fix, code, $0 (the sink of D264): `extraction.narrowest_links`, applied in `file_reading` to every filing from v20 on: a statement linked to a question and to a question that question depends on (the ledger's `dependencies`, the seeds' root-and-driver pairs, transitively) keeps the narrower one only, which is D207's \"narrowest question only\" made an identity rule where the ledger knows the hierarchy. Replayed over the three v92 ledgers: links 967/921/907 → removed 302/310/285 (31–34%), no statement left without a link (the rule keeps the narrower); the three revenue questions' share and the per-question piles after the rule are printed in `design-v72.md` §9. Test `test_a_statement_filed_under_a_driver_and_its_root_keeps_the_driver_only`.\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md-3089-- What the rule does not do: a statement whose only link is a revenue question it does not bear on (the reactor output, the optical plant) stays there; that is the extraction's noise class and the figure-line clause (D264's first mechanism), the next class.\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md-3090-- The second fix, text, proved for cents (D264's second mechanism, the supporting matters v66's check removes): the model's own account on six of the twenty lost matters (`probe-v72-missing-supporting.txt`) cited in three cases a check row whose own boundary should have sent the statement back (an arrangement in place against a new step; common knowledge without a figure against a competitor's share with a figure; a product detail against a delay of the product that carries the value), and those three boundaries were the ones written without an example. `review-v73.txt` (role and categories identical to v72's; `poc/config/poc-v93.json`) gives each its kept-side example in another domain and drops the row-1 clause the header already states: 3,548 → 3,822 characters, the reason being AGENTS §6's rule that a classification is a closed set with examples. Proof (`harness/resend_review_v73.py`, `proof-review-v73.txt`: the 17 articles of the 20 matters, three sends each under poc-v93 from v92 draw 1's snapshots, against the three stored v92 draws): the 20 matters appear 10 → 28 times of 60, present in at least two sends 0 → 11, the three probed cases 0/3, 1/3, 0/3 → 2/3, 3/3, 3/3; the guard, gold not-kept statements written on the same 17 articles, 0.47 → 0.61 per article per send (about 2.4 more per 17 articles against 6 more supporting matters per send). Not a patch by that ratio, but under v72 what the extraction writes reaches the judge, so the whole bench decides: three draws of poc-v93 with the narrowest rule against the v92 baseline (about $2.7) at his word. Not decided: whether poc-v93 replaces poc-v92 as the default.\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md-3091-\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md-3092-## D266 · 2026-11-02 · Three quick fixes on the v72 base, each proved on stored data in minutes, put together as poc-v94 and run once: the retold-arrangement noise, the quote refusals, and the judgement churn that was not one\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md-3093-\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md-3094-- Alex, on the five classes listed after the v72 measurement: \"2/4/5比较重要，快速验证。不要drift,不要跑超级繁琐的全方位验证，先poc 改，能work,有结论，全部改动放到一起再跑完整\". (And on the first version of that list: \"你讲的tmd是人话吗？…再给我讲Ai黑话我就干死你\": every message to him is plain language, AGENTS \"Authority and scope\".)\n--\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md-3510-- Mechanism: the state chip and the chart's spoken text join the score and the rung label. A two-rung ladder's score is Yes/No; when the ladder names its outcomes (06-views allows named outcomes for yes/no theme theses), the label repeats it. Census: 1 of 55 two-rung theses in the served ledger (v49: Restriction adopted / No restriction adopted) and 1 in the 2026-10-27 snapshot (Permission granted / Permission not granted).\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md-3511-- `stateWords` in `poc/ui/src/model/thesis.js` owns what a state shows: a two-rung ladder shows its own outcome once; five-rung ladders keep score and label. `badgeHtml` and `stateText` read it. Tone, lanes, the score table and the composite still use the Yes/No score.\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md-3512-- Result: the D336 UI test fails on the old composition (\"No No restriction adopted\"); 58 UI tests, lint, format and the 20 standing UI mutation checks pass. In headless Chrome, with the cache disabled, v49 shows \"No restriction adopted\" and v14 \"Yes\".\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md-3513-\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md-3514-## Decisions recorded in the `main` checkout on 2026-10-27 and never committed (numbered at the 2026-11-03 cleanup)\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md-3515-\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md-3516-These sixteen decisions (the Lightsail server, the single-call stability study, the source and routing studies, the Vera case, the\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md-3517-cleaned page database and the TrueNorth event index) were written in the `main` checkout as D242–D257 on 2026-10-27 and stayed\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:3518:uncommitted while both lines moved on. At the cleanup (D353) they were committed in order under new numbers: D242→D337, D243→D338, D244→D339, D245→D340, D246→D341, D247→D342, D248→D343, D249→D344, D250→D345, D251→D346, D252→D347, D253→D348, D254→D349, D255→D350, D256→D351, D257→D352. Their\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md-3519-research documents came with them; the experiment outputs and runner scripts they link to were never committed and are kept only in\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md-3520-the backup named in D353.\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md-3521-\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md-3522-## D337 · 2026-10-27 · Create the Singapore Lightsail development server\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md-3523-\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md-3524-- Alex requested the USD 44/month Singapore Lightsail server after a final footprint check for extraction, Docker and frontend serving. Provision one `large_3_0` Ubuntu 24.04 instance with dedicated SSH access and an attached static IP. Docker and private read-only application verification are part of server readiness.\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md-3525-- This starts infrastructure only. Paid extraction, public model-backed API deployment, provider-credential transfer, additional paid services and unfinished product publication are outside this slice. Model charges and optional storage/transfer extras remain separate from the server bundle. The [operation record](research/2026-10-27-lightsail.md) owns configuration, measurements and verification.\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md-3526-\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md-3527-## D338 · 2026-10-27 · Test single-call extraction stability by correcting the task and preserving the request\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md-3528-\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md-3529-- Alex explicitly rejects voting across repeated answers and requests stability tests plus correction of contradictory extraction instructions, with a hedge-fund analyst's judgement. Repeated calls measure independent answers; they never form one production answer.\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md-3530-- The [development study](research/2026-10-27-extraction-stability/plan.md) uses the admission-v12 worktree's runtime and three preserved benchmark articles. It crosses the original versus analyst prompt with original versus reporting-only text, five independent calls per cell, with exact HTTP request bytes preserved. The original property order is reconstructed because the earlier archive's canonical JSON reordered the schema before re-sending it.\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md-3531-- The candidate clarifies that a source-grounded business driver can inform an outcome without being that outcome, preserves customer/supplier identity and plan/actual distinctions, and routes a segment fact to the most specific shown question. It remains an isolated research prompt. Candidate admission, grouping, downstream behaviour and the production default do not change in this study.\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md-3532-- Freeze source-claim annotations before calls, report every sample, inspect meaning as well as coverage, and retain failures. At most 60 single-attempt calls and $1.50 of conservative study accounting; no earlier budget is changed. The long extraction run stays paused. Results establish only what these fixed development cases show.\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md-3533-- Completed: [all 60 samples and diagnosis](research/2026-10-27-extraction-stability/results.md). The candidate does not provide an overall stability improvement and is not promoted. The study also identifies displayed-but-unusable thesis IDs, schema-permitted empty links, and punctuation-space quote refusals; these remain explicit open defects, not a claim that sampling alone explains the failures. No further arm or production change is implied by this result.\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md-3534-\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md-3535-## D339 · 2026-10-27 · Measure a source/route extraction POC against Luna and DeepSeek\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md-3536-\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md-3537-- Alex requests a small implemented and measured POC, following discussion of extraction stability and DeepSeek V4.1 Flash. The [frozen study](research/2026-10-27-extraction-contract-poc/plan.md) compares the original task with separate source reading and routing, on three existing development articles, three independent results per configuration. Repeated outputs never vote or combine.\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md-3538-- The research path uses source locations copied by code, a required answer per source paragraph, and a required explicit destination per extracted observation. Pending observations remain visible in the research record and are not successful library delivery. Existing production checks are exercised separately so their drops and merges remain visible.\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md-3539-- Compare gpt-6-luna low with deepseek-flash non-thinking at temperature 0 through its strict tool interface. This compares deployable configurations, not isolated model weights. Up to 54 scheduled HTTP calls and a combined $1.50 conservative budget; failed sandbox DNS attempts are preserved and their reservations reduce the host-run budget. No production default, frozen module contract, candidate/group construction, matching, judging or long-run status changes.\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md-3540-- The initial research adapter incorrectly assumed one tool call per response. All nine DeepSeek source responses instead contain disjoint pieces of the complete required object. The [protocol repair](research/2026-10-27-extraction-contract-poc/protocol-repair.md) validates their combined object from each single stored response and is intended to complete only the nine unsent routing calls, using the same prompts and labels. Original failures remain; no source request is resent. Report this post-observation adapter repair and both stages' complete cost, rather than describing the result as an unchanged registered comparison.\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md-3541-- Alex explicitly stopped the session and requested a restart log. The [handoff](research/2026-10-27-extraction-contract-poc/HANDOFF.md) records 49 received model responses, four additional connection failures without responses, and five unsent routing steps. Two of the four received repaired-route responses are malformed; the runner incorrectly halted remaining admission on those local parse failures. All failures remain. Estimated response cost is $0.130202088; combined conservative charges and unknown reservations are $0.407739 under the unchanged $1.50 ceiling. Analysis and final verification are unfinished. No new calls or tests follow the stop instruction.\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md-3542-\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md-3543-- Alex resumed: “keep on testing” and asked whether the errors came from model use and extraction/processing design. [Completed results](research/2026-10-27-extraction-contract-poc/results.md): only the five unsent route steps were sent, with original requests and the same $1.50 ceiling. Final totals: 54 responses plus four preserved connection failures, estimated $0.153860676, conservative charges/reservations $0.451203. Three malformed route answers remain failures. The bounded runner now distinguishes local validation failure from transport/unknown usage.\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md-3544-- Separated source reading retains 18/18 labelled core claims in each repeat for both providers; that does not establish full pipeline correctness. Three same-quote merges erase distinct summaries; an offline replay restores exactly those three. All 31 positive labels expect `v6`, so target recall alone cannot establish routing specificity. The source/routing preservation contract and a balanced routing measure are proposed next decisions, not adopted product changes. Frozen modules, defaults and the paused long run remain unchanged.\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md-3545-\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md-3546-\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md-3547-## D340 · 2026-10-27 · Specify the source stage and research routing/admission before more model runs\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md-3548-\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md-3549-- Alex requests an explicit subagent task to define the separated first stage precisely, while continuing a deeper study of routing, accuracy and uncontrolled thesis accumulation. This authorizes isolated research, not adoption of a new frozen module contract or a new paid arm.\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md-3550-- The [source contract candidate](research/2026-10-27-source-contract-v2/design.md) audits all 18 D339 source responses / 553 records. Its isolated schema and checks require original-text references for claimant and time mentions and remove model-generated publisher identity. Exact references reject invented text but do not establish semantic correctness; anonymous-expert tier meaning and downstream date adaptation remain open. No historical records or labels are rewritten.\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md-3551-- The [routing study](research/2026-10-27-routing-design/proposal.md) reads two stored ledgers and 171 candidate decisions. The default v23 has 95 new decisions among 102 candidates; 23 new decisions include a raw part-of relation, and 22 of those were written. These are exposure counts, not confirmed erroneous admissions. The proposed rule separates business relevance, question identity and independent significance, so failure to match is not automatic permission to create a thesis.\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md-3552-- Removing the mandatory numeric-card recipe changes a D62 tradeoff and is not adopted by this research record. No hard-coded aggregate merging, company quotas, new review queue, model switch, production edit, commit, push, deployment or long-run restart is authorized. Agree on source and balanced routing/admission semantic cases before fixing the final interface and measuring a fresh candidate against controls. This slice adds no model expense.\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md-3553-\n--\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md-3940-- Done: `docs/DECISIONS.md` states what is in force, by module in PRD order, with the choices open for Alex, the conflicts settled by\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md-3941-  reading the decisions together, and an index of every decision number's status. The full records moved unchanged to this file\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md-3942-  (D163: nothing historical is rewritten); the frontend's presentation decisions in force are listed in `docs/DECISIONS-frontend.md`.\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md-3943-  Each of the 365 decisions was classified by a first reader (four Claude readers, one range each) and the classification checked\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md-3944-  against this log by a second (Codex, eleven ranges); the records, checks and scripts are in\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md-3945-  `docs/research/2026-11-05-decisions-consolidation/`.\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md-3946-- Corrections recorded here instead of in the entries: D366's \"every run since D256\" means D351 (`main`'s D256 before the merge\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md-3947-  numbering). AGENTS and the README called the extraction standard page \"version 3\"; the page is version 5 (version 3 as signed in D243,\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:3948:  with D248's seven boundaries and D250's four evidence boundaries and counting unit). AGENTS §8 named `golden-v3-signed.json`; the\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md-3949-  frozen gold is golden-v5 (D261). AGENTS placed the frozen ruler's files in the extraction worktree; they are in `main`.\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md-3950-- AGENTS.md keeps every rule at its decision with Alex's words; the incident narratives behind the rules are left to this log; the\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md-3951-  extraction-ruler bullet joined §7.1; \"own the loop\" now reads with \"a run starts only on his word\" and D355's stop rule; §11 says how a\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md-3952-  decision is recorded. The README, `docs/CURRENT_STATE.md` and `docs/poc/pipeline-plan.md` describe the current pipeline; the PRDs and\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md-3953-  design-page passages that contradicted decisions in force were corrected.\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md-3954-- Reviewed in seven rounds of read-only Codex review by angle (the register against this log, AGENTS new against old, the PRDs and design\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md-3955-  page against the decisions in force, the guides against the code and runs); serious findings per round 30, 9 (and 13 classes in the\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md-3956-  PRDs), 7, 7, 3, 6 and 5, each checked against its source before a change; after the last, only PRD 10's two lines remain, left for\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md-3957-  Alex. Found on the way: the default Jev path chooses no dependencies although D51 has matching choose them.\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md-3958-- Open for Alex: the seven items at the head of `docs/DECISIONS.md`.\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md-3959-\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md-3960-## D368 · 2026-11-05 · Alex's answers to the seven items left open by the consolidation\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md-3961-\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md-3962-- Alex, on the seven items at the head of `docs/DECISIONS.md` (D367): \"1. 这个你记住，我们要做 2. 做 3. 好那就按照后面的那条来 4. 好你来定 5. 你要来帮我看到底做不做\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md-3963-  6. 你看该怎么处理核实 7. 不，用英文吧。\"; then \"你开始逐条改，不要drift, 记录下来把1-7都清理了我们再commit push,开始快速做\".\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md-3964-- Decided:\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md-3965-  1. The asset-thesis rungs stated against guidance, each thesis naming its favourable end (D186), and the rename of `industry_aggregate`\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md-3966-     to `shared_quantity` (D191 point 4) are built in the next extraction version. The frozen v74i stays until then (D274); the new\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md-3967-     version is measured against it.\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md-3968-  2. The three decided rules not yet built are built, each designed and measured as its own slice (AGENTS §2, §7): a company's own\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md-3969-     quantity is a thesis under that company, private companies included (D187); a later item may add a dependency to an existing thesis\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md-3970-     (D191 point 2); the matching step chooses a new thesis's dependencies (D51), which the default Jev path does not ask today.\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:3971:  3. At the due day pull mode closes the due questions and does nothing else (D356); D248 boundary 2's step that opens the next-deadline\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md-3972-     successor of an event question falling due unresolved is dropped.\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md-3973-  4. Settled by Claude on Alex's delegation, by D208's design: a seed question's dependency arrow means \"supports\". For filing, the\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md-3974-     supporting (driver) question is the narrower one, so a statement linked to both goes to it, as `extraction.narrowest_links` does\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md-3975-     today. For judging, the supported (root) question reads the supporting questions' conclusions, so drivers and themes are judged\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md-3976-     before their roots. Today the judging code reads the stored edge the other way: the driver reads the root and is judged after it\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md-3977-     (`seeding.seed_views` stores the seed's `depends_on` as the driver's dependency). The fix separates the two uses of the edge; it\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md-3978-     changes judgements, so it is measured before it enters the default.\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md-3979-  5. Settled by Claude on Alex's delegation: PRD 10 is corrected without changing any rule. §4 names the frozen standard's version 5 and\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md-3980-     §5 carries a status line (its links-rule version failed in §8 step 5; D361 keeps the fallback sentence).\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md-3981-  6. Settled by Claude on Alex's delegation: the three statements of the frozen extraction standard page that later decisions changed are\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md-3982-     noted in a dated correction record beside it, `docs/prd/05-extraction-standard-corrections.md`; the page is not edited (D261). Each\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md-3983-     statement was found verbatim in the page: \"抽取看不到库\" (§4 and §5.3; changed by D251 and D264), \"研究的交付物是论证\" (§7; the\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md-3984-     argument record set aside on 2026-11-04) and \"只有事实能确定落在哪一档\" (§5 and §7; changed by D260 and D263).\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md-3985-  7. Pages written for Alex's review are in English, like the rest of the maintained documentation (D163); PRD 10 is translated, his\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md-3986-     quotes kept in their own language. What is said to him keeps the plain-language rule (AGENTS, Authority and scope).\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md-3987-- Recorded in the same change: `docs/DECISIONS.md` (the open items cleared into their sections), AGENTS §11, the README, PRD 10, the\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md-3988-  correction record and `docs/CURRENT_STATE.md` (the builds of items 1, 2 and 4 are the next tasks, in an order given there).\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md-3989-\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md-3990-## D369 · 2026-11-05 UTC · Capture core and supporting evidence without a strict boundary; retain the MXC case\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md-3991-\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md-3992-- Alex: “我觉得往后核心和辅助其实只要是捕捉到就好，不用真的严格区分了，把它作为decision, 因为这两个边界很模糊，我觉得没必要纠结到死” and “我觉得留下辅助，只要LLM自己的判断是相关且逻辑清晰就好”.\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md-3993-- For future extraction evaluation, evidence that the standard would keep as core or supporting is assessed together for whether it was captured. Do not make a hard pass/fail distinction between those two weights. This does not establish that every statement is relevant, change the optional or excluded boundary, replace source tiers, or remove checks for meaning, attribution, uncertainty, errors and delivery. Historical scores retain their original definitions and are not compared as if this was their ruler.\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md-3994-- In the reviewed Microsoft MXC example, retain the reported announcement as supporting evidence. The model may judge relevance using a clear logical connection; an unquantified indirect connection is not automatically rejected. A proposed NVIDIA demand effect is an inference, not a fact attributed to Microsoft; the article does not say MXC requires NVIDIA hardware. This is not permission to accept unrelated material or to hard-code a list or new mandatory output field.\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md-3995-- The frozen standard v5, golden-v5, seeds and historical results remain byte-for-byte unchanged (D261/D262). Applying this decision to a new real-article gold requires a separate evaluation version under D261. Alex asked for a real-article gold; treating that as authorization to develop the separate version is an implementation interpretation, not a quotation from his decision. It still needs its own traced references, independent review and Alex's sign-off before scoring. The experimental evidence comparison has not been sent.\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md-3996-\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md-3997-\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md-3998-## D370 · 2026-11-05 UTC · Remove the separate earnings-report import\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md-3999-\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md-4000-- Alex: “我觉得财报这个基本是没有的，我觉得可以记录下，删除这个财报倒入的环节。重新整理现在的系统设计”. He also previously directed removal of the 22 artificial preset questions and confirmed that extraction should read the existing research library.\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md-4001-- Remove the separate coverage-start report reading tied to seeded questions and do not add an earnings report as background to each news extraction request. This supersedes D363–D366 to the extent they require that separate report import and seeded default. An earnings release or filing arriving as an actual input remains a normal item under D28; existing research questions remain extraction context. Historical seeds, gold, results and records remain historical, not a new active starting library.\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md-4002-- Evidence is bounded: a diagnostic with three archived NVDA articles, the same 68-question 2026-08-28 library, two arms and three draws gave 14/27 complete matters without the appended report versus 13/27 with it; one report-arm answer supplied an unestablished CFO statement date. This tested adding a report to extraction, not the distinct D363–D366 coverage-start mechanism; the removal of both is Alex's decision, not a claim that the experiment directly tested both. The library is historical and not the complete article-day state. See `../hivemind-no-preseed-evidence-review/docs/research/2026-11-05-real-input-evidence/existing-library-results-2026-11-05.md` in the local worktree.\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md-4003-- Implementation and rollout status must be stated separately from this decision. The frozen earlier rulers and scores stay unchanged; no conclusion about other companies or report-as-source inputs is implied.\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md-4004-\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md-4005-\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md-4006-## D371 · 2026-11-05 UTC · Track present and forward-looking financial information\n--\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md-4169-  The link recheck covered the 34 disputed links and 10 accepted links as controls (all useful); the other 49 fresh links were not\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md-4170-  rechecked.\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md-4171-\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md-4172-## D388 · 2026-11-09 · A material unsigned obligation gets its own signing question beside an open total of its kind\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md-4173-\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md-4174-- Asked: \"一笔重大的、还没签的承诺（比如为 OpenAI 俄亥俄数据中心租约做担保），要不要在已有的'担保总额'问题之外，单独开一个'会不会签'的问题？\"\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md-4175-  Alex chose \"单独开 (Recommended)\".\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md-4176-- **Decided.** A material unsigned obligation that merits a separate investment judgment keeps its own yes/no question on whether\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:4177:  it is signed by the check date, beside an open question on the total of the same kind. This confirms D248 boundary 1's exception,\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md-4178-  which had not been put to him. A small unsigned obligation, or a deal already signed under a plan tracked by amount, stays evidence\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md-4179-  for the total.\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md-4180-- **Why it matters now.** The c8 dev draws fold the Ohio guarantee into the aggregate in 3 of 3, and q23 of the frozen judgement gold\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md-4181-  asks it. Arm c9 showed that a sentence-level rule flips by send (round log §§48–50).\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md-4182-- **Next.** A structural lever, designed and reviewed by the council before any send. c8 stays in force until a version is shown to\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md-4183-  be better on new, unused articles.\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md-4184-\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md-4185-## D389 · 2026-11-09 · An unsigned obligation is large enough for its own signing question at about 5% of the company's annual profit\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md-4186-\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md-4187-- Asked: \"“多大算大”用什么尺寸？\" The options were 5% of a year's profit (recommended), 1% of annual revenue, or no threshold and stop.\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md-4188-  Alex chose \"一年利润的 5% (Recommended)\", whose stated terms were:\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md-4189-  - \"单笔未签承诺约达到公司一年利润的 5% 才单独开'会不会签'（亏损公司另议）\";\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md-4190-  - \"金额不知道的，比如俄亥俄，仍按文章描述定性判断\";\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md-4191-  - \"公司最近一年利润作为固定资料交给小步骤\".\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md-4192-- **Decided.** Under D388, a single unsigned obligation is large enough for its own signing question when its stated amount is about 5%\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md-4193-  or more of the company's most recent annual profit. An obligation whose amount is not stated is judged qualitatively from what the\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md-4194-  item states. The company's most recent annual profit is supplied to the step as fixed input, with its source. A loss-making company\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md-4195-  is not covered and is decided when one arises.\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md-4196-- **Why.** In the focused D388 call, the same $2bn stake opened in 0 of 3 draws under one wording and 3 of 3 under another, and a\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md-4197-  $2.5–3bn stake opened in 6 of 6, even when compared with stated revenue (round log §§54–55). The standard's \"large enough to change\"\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:4198:  (D248 boundary 6) had no anchor the model applied consistently. The 5% line agrees with every known verdict:\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md-4199-  - small: about $2bn, $2.5–3bn, Intel's $5bn;\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md-4200-  - open: Hugging Face at $12.9bn.\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md-4201-- **Scope.** It applies to the focused D388 step under test. It enters the clean-arch PRD only if that step is adopted. The frozen\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md-4202-  extraction standard and gold are unchanged (AGENTS §7.1).\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md-4203-\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md-4204-## D390 · 2026-11-09 · A plan counts as undertaken once a deal under it is reported signed\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md-4205-\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md-4206-- Asked: \"一个合作计划，什么时候算'已经启动'（只跟踪总额，不再问'会不会签'）？\" The options were: started once a deal under it is\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md-4207-  signed (recommended); started only when the company announces the whole plan in effect; or stop. Alex chose \"已有交易签了就算启动\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md-4208-  (Recommended)\", whose stated terms were:\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md-4209-  - \"文章报道计划下已经有交易签了，就把整个计划当作已经启动，只用'总额'问题跟踪\";\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md-4210-  - \"单笔还没签的大交易（如俄亥俄）照样单独问\";\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md-4211-  - \"代价：'试点签了、大计划未定'这种罕见情况会被当成已启动\".\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md-4212-- **Decided.** Under D388, a programme or plan as a whole counts as undertaken once the item reports a deal signed under it. It is then\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md-4213-  tracked by its amount, the total of its kind, and gets no signing question of its own. Each single deal within it keeps its own\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md-4214-  status, so a material unsigned deal under such a plan still gets its own signing question.\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md-4215-- **Why.** In the focused D388 call, dev-20 turned NVIDIA's announced credit-support model into a signing question in 2 of 3 rounds,\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md-4216-  although the same article reports Sharon AI's signed agreement under it; a blind reader judged it already signed. Three fix drafts\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md-4217-  were blocked because the standard (\"已经承担（一笔或一个计划）：金额\") does not say when a whole plan is undertaken (round log §57).\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md-4218-- **Scope.** It applies to the focused D388 step under test and enters the clean-arch PRD only if that step is adopted. The frozen\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md-4219-  standard and gold are unchanged.\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md-4220-\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md-4221-## D391 · 2026-11-09 · Close clean Step 1 on c8; state each change's effect on the judgement first\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md-4222-\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md-4223-- Alex: \"感觉现在一直在修一些mknor的原地打转，你是不是要思考下现在具体还差什么high priority big impact 的需要做？还是要收尾step-\".\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md-4224-  After the priorities council (round log §59), to \"第 1 步收尾，并开始整条链的测量？\" he answered \"收尾，你先完整的和council\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md-4225-  讨论下你要怎么做下一步的收尾测量等，需要你完整的读完trace 和所有历史的learning 和我们的状态再决定下一步\". To the proposed working\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md-4226-  rule he answered \"写进去 (Recommended)\".\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md-4227-- **Decided:**\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md-4228-  - **Clean Step 1 is closed on c8 (D387).** The focused D388 call is a tested candidate, not adopted. It opened Ohio in 36 of 36\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md-4229-    draws, but each round opened one wrong neighbouring case (§§54–58); D389 and D390 apply to it only. The open defects are listed in\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md-4230-    `docs/CURRENT_STATE.md`.\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md-4231-  - **New rule (AGENTS §7.3, \"Name the effect on the judgement first\").** Every proposed change states its expected effect on a reader\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md-4232-    or on the final judgement, and is tested there where possible. A fix that keeps moving its error to neighbouring cases stops being\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md-4233-    tuned on that set.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_1","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"rg -n '\"'^## D248'\"' docs/DECISIONS-log.md && cat clean-arch/unseeded-2026-11-10/opened-dev.json clean-arch/unseeded-2026-11-10/ruler-questions.json\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_1","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"rg -n '\"'^## D248'\"' docs/DECISIONS-log.md && cat clean-arch/unseeded-2026-11-10/opened-dev.json clean-arch/unseeded-2026-11-10/ruler-questions.json\"","aggregated_output":"2954:## D248 · 2026-10-30 · What counts as one question and one piece of evidence: seven boundaries, chosen one by one\n[\n {\n  \"run\": \"dev-d1\",\n  \"id\": \"clean-1\",\n  \"article\": 1,\n  \"description\": \"How much credit support will NVIDIA have extended to AI cloud partners for their financing or capacity commitments, as disclosed in its filings, by the check date?\",\n  \"outcome\": \"The amount and form of credit support, guarantees or similar obligations NVIDIA discloses for AI cloud partners.\",\n  \"period\": \"By 2027-12-31, a check date within 18 months of the item, using NVIDIA's annual report and quarterly filings.\"\n },\n {\n  \"run\": \"dev-d1\",\n  \"id\": \"clean-2\",\n  \"article\": 24,\n  \"description\": \"Will NVIDIA's Vera Rubin next-generation AI chip platform begin shipping by the end of calendar 2026?\",\n  \"outcome\": \"First shipments of NVIDIA's Vera Rubin AI chip platform.\",\n  \"period\": \"By 2026-12-31 (calendar year-end; the item says Vera Rubin is in full production and 'could begin shipping later this year').\"\n },\n {\n  \"run\": \"dev-d1\",\n  \"id\": \"clean-3\",\n  \"article\": 30,\n  \"description\": \"Will the Chinese government permit Nvidia to sell its H200 AI chips in China, allowing Nvidia to resume China data-center chip sales, by the check date?\",\n  \"outcome\": \"A decision by China's government to allow — or continue blocking — Nvidia H200 AI-chip sales in China.\",\n  \"period\": \"By Nvidia's fiscal year-end in late January 2027 (the current fiscal year-end fixed by the item's July 2026 date, per the pending-regulatory-decision default).\"\n },\n {\n  \"run\": \"dev-d1\",\n  \"id\": \"clean-4\",\n  \"article\": 42,\n  \"description\": \"Will the four largest AI hyperscalers' combined data-center capital expenditures reach roughly $1 trillion in calendar 2027, up from about $650 billion planned for calendar 2026?\",\n  \"outcome\": \"The four largest AI hyperscalers' combined calendar-2027 data-center capital expenditures, versus the ~$650 billion planned for calendar 2026.\",\n  \"period\": \"Calendar 2027; check after the four hyperscalers report Q4 2027 results (early 2028), the release date of the aggregate annual capex figures.\"\n },\n {\n  \"run\": \"dev-d1\",\n  \"id\": \"clean-5\",\n  \"article\": 49,\n  \"description\": \"Will Nvidia's Kyber rack-scale architecture, the rack system designed to house its Vera Rubin Ultra chips, begin shipping by the end of calendar 2028, after SemiAnalysis reported a delay of more than 12 months to 2028?\",\n  \"outcome\": \"First shipments of Nvidia's Kyber rack-scale architecture / Vera Rubin Ultra systems.\",\n  \"period\": \"By 2028-12-31 (SemiAnalysis reports the Kyber/Rubin Ultra debut pushed from 2027 to 2028).\"\n },\n {\n  \"run\": \"dev-d1\",\n  \"id\": \"clean-6\",\n  \"article\": 59,\n  \"description\": \"How large will NVIDIA's supply purchase commitments be at its next annual report, and how much of that obligation is tied to AI capacity that must be absorbed?\",\n  \"outcome\": \"NVIDIA's total purchase and supply commitments disclosed in its annual report (and updated in 10-Qs).\",\n  \"period\": \"At NVIDIA's next annual report (fiscal-2027 Form 10-K, expected around February 2027; the obligation is already undertaken, so it is tracked by its amount at the next annual report).\"\n },\n {\n  \"run\": \"dev-d1\",\n  \"id\": \"clean-7\",\n  \"article\": 87,\n  \"description\": \"Will Chinese enterprises shift roughly 46% of their AI-accelerator budgets to domestic suppliers within the next 12 months, up from about 30% today, reducing demand for Nvidia-class imported accelerators?\",\n  \"outcome\": \"The share of Chinese AI-accelerator budgets allocated to domestic suppliers within 12 months, versus roughly 30% today.\",\n  \"period\": \"By 2027-07-07, within 12 months of the July 2026 item (the next calendar year); settled by the next industry survey release.\"\n },\n {\n  \"run\": \"dev-d1\",\n  \"id\": \"clean-8\",\n  \"article\": 94,\n  \"description\": \"Will DRAM and NAND memory-chip contract prices at the end of calendar 2027 be higher than at the end of calendar 2026 — i.e., will the memory shortage Micron says could last until 2028 keep prices elevated through next year?\",\n  \"outcome\": \"End-2027 DRAM/NAND contract price levels versus end-2026, and whether memory supply remains tight through calendar 2027.\",\n  \"period\": \"Calendar 2027; checked against Q4 2027 memory contract-price assessments published in early 2028 (release date of the aggregate price the thesis tracks).\"\n },\n {\n  \"run\": \"dev-d2\",\n  \"id\": \"clean-1\",\n  \"article\": 1,\n  \"description\": \"How much credit support (guarantees or credit enhancement for AI cloud partners' infrastructure financing) will NVIDIA have extended under its revenue-sharing and credit-support model by its next annual report?\",\n  \"outcome\": \"The disclosed amount of credit support or guarantee exposure NVIDIA has committed to AI cloud partners under the new revenue-sharing and credit-support model.\",\n  \"period\": \"NVIDIA's next annual report (FY2027 Form 10-K, fiscal year ending late January 2027); set as the reporting date for an obligation being undertaken, per section 3.\"\n },\n {\n  \"run\": \"dev-d2\",\n  \"id\": \"clean-2\",\n  \"article\": 24,\n  \"description\": \"Will NVIDIA's next-generation Vera Rubin AI chip platform, the product line that carries its data center value, reach first customer shipments by the end of 2026?\",\n  \"outcome\": \"First shipments of NVIDIA's Vera Rubin platform occurring by end-2026, as the item says shipments 'could begin later this year'.\",\n  \"period\": \"2026 year-end; set from the item's statement that Vera Rubin could begin shipping 'later this year' (2026), checked against NVIDIA's quarterly results and shipment/availability confirmations during the year.\"\n },\n {\n  \"run\": \"dev-d2\",\n  \"id\": \"clean-3\",\n  \"article\": 30,\n  \"description\": \"Will Beijing permit imports/sales of Nvidia's H200 AI chips into China by Nvidia's FY2027 year-end?\",\n  \"outcome\": \"A Chinese government decision (or continuation of the ban) on allowing Nvidia H200 AI-chip sales into China.\",\n  \"period\": \"Nvidia's FY2027 year-end (fiscal year ending late January 2027); the item gives no date for China's decision, so this pending regulatory decision is checked at the current fiscal year-end, per section 3.\"\n },\n {\n  \"run\": \"dev-d2\",\n  \"id\": \"clean-4\",\n  \"article\": 42,\n  \"description\": \"Will the four largest AI hyperscalers' combined data center capital expenditures reach roughly $1 trillion in calendar 2027, up from about $650 billion planned for 2026, as NVIDIA projects?\",\n  \"outcome\": \"The combined 2027 data center capital expenditures of the four largest AI hyperscalers, measured against NVIDIA's projection that the figure could reach $1 trillion.\",\n  \"period\": \"Calendar 2027; confirmed when the four hyperscalers report full-year 2027 capital expenditures in their Q4-2027/annual filings (early 2028). Set from the item's 'next year ... $1 trillion' projection.\"\n },\n {\n  \"run\": \"dev-d2\",\n  \"id\": \"clean-5\",\n  \"article\": 49,\n  \"description\": \"Will Nvidia's Kyber rack-scale architecture for Vera Rubin Ultra (the NVL144 rack system housing its 2027 Rubin Ultra chips) reach first customer shipments in 2027 as originally planned, or slip to 2028 as SemiAnalysis reports?\",\n  \"outcome\": \"Timing of first customer shipments of Nvidia's Kyber NVL144 rack system for Vera Rubin Ultra — 2027 (as originally slated) versus 2028 (as SemiAnalysis reports).\",\n  \"period\": \"2027–2028; the item reports the debut slipped from 2027 to 2028, checked against Nvidia's shipment/availability confirmations in its quarterly results and product disclosures.\"\n },\n {\n  \"run\": \"dev-d2\",\n  \"id\": \"clean-6\",\n  \"article\": 59,\n  \"description\": \"How large will NVIDIA's supply purchase commitments (obligations to buy memory, components and capacity) be at its next annual report, after the company was reported to carry $119 billion of supply commitments?\",\n  \"outcome\": \"The dollar amount of NVIDIA's supply purchase commitments disclosed in its FY2027 Form 10-K, measured against the $119 billion the item reports.\",\n  \"period\": \"NVIDIA's next annual report (FY2027 Form 10-K, fiscal year ending late January 2027); set as the reporting date for an obligation already undertaken, per section 3.\"\n },\n {\n  \"run\": \"dev-d2\",\n  \"id\": \"clean-7\",\n  \"article\": 71,\n  \"description\": \"Will Nvidia's Rubin Ultra GPUs — now a dual-chiplet part after the reported switch from a quad-chiplet design — reach first customer shipments in calendar 2027 as the item indicates they are slated to?\",\n  \"outcome\": \"First customer shipments of Nvidia's Rubin Ultra GPUs occurring in 2027, whether in Oberon racks while the Kyber rack slips to 2028 or in Kyber.\",\n  \"period\": \"Calendar 2027; set from the item's references to \\\"2027's Rubin Ultra GPUs\\\" and to the Kyber rack (reported delayed to 2028) as the cabinet \\\"meant for\\\" them, checked against Nvidia's quarterly results and product availability/shipment confirmations during 2027.\"\n },\n {\n  \"run\": \"dev-d2\",\n  \"id\": \"clean-8\",\n  \"article\": 85,\n  \"description\": \"Will the U.S. Congress enact legislation to phase out Chinese-made lidar sensors — including Hesai's, which the item says is one option automakers can integrate into Nvidia's DRIVE Hyperion autonomous-vehicle platform — in the United States by Nvidia's FY2027 year-end?\",\n  \"outcome\": \"Enactment (or failure) of U.S. legislation phasing out Chinese-made lidar (e.g., Hesai's) from U.S. autonomous systems, which would remove a low-cost lidar option from Nvidia's autonomous-vehicle platform.\",\n  \"period\": \"Nvidia's FY2027 year-end (fiscal year ending late January 2027); the item gives no date for the proposed legislation, so per section 3 the pending regulatory decision is checked at the current fiscal year-end.\"\n },\n {\n  \"run\": \"dev-d2\",\n  \"id\": \"clean-9\",\n  \"article\": 87,\n  \"description\": \"Will Chinese firms shift 46% of their AI-accelerator budgets to domestic suppliers within 12 months (by mid-2027), up from roughly 30% today, reducing Nvidia's addressable China accelerator demand?\",\n  \"outcome\": \"The share of Chinese firms' AI-accelerator budgets allocated to domestic suppliers, measured against the survey's 46% target within 12 months.\",\n  \"period\": \"Within 12 months of the July 2026 item (by mid-2027); set from the survey's 'within 12 months' horizon, checked against the next industry survey and Nvidia's China revenue disclosures.\"\n },\n {\n  \"run\": \"dev-d2\",\n  \"id\": \"clean-10\",\n  \"article\": 91,\n  \"description\": \"Will the U.S. Commerce Department's inquiry into whether Chinese AI firm DeepSeek obtained restricted Nvidia chips through Singapore/Malaysia intermediaries result in a public enforcement action or new export restriction affecting Nvidia's China business (e.g., findings, entity-list designations, or tighter transshipment controls) by Nvidia's FY2027 year-end?\",\n  \"outcome\": \"A public U.S. Commerce Department/BIS finding, enforcement action, or new export restriction stemming from the DeepSeek/diversion-of-Nvidia-chips inquiry, versus no such action.\",\n  \"period\": \"Nvidia's FY2027 year-end (fiscal year ending late January 2027); the item gives no date for the Commerce inquiry's conclusion, so this pending regulatory matter is checked at the current fiscal year-end, per section 3.\"\n },\n {\n  \"run\": \"dev-d3\",\n  \"id\": \"clean-1\",\n  \"article\": 1,\n  \"description\": \"How much credit support will NVIDIA have extended to AI cloud partners under the revenue-sharing and credit-support model it is introducing, as disclosed in its guarantee and commitment disclosures?\",\n  \"outcome\": \"The amount of credit support / backstop exposure NVIDIA has extended to AI cloud partners' infrastructure financing, as reported in NVIDIA's filings.\",\n  \"period\": \"NVIDIA's next annual report — FY2027 Form 10-K for the fiscal year ending late January 2027, expected filed around February 2027 (set by the reason: an obligation already undertaken is tracked by its amount at the next annual report).\"\n },\n {\n  \"run\": \"dev-d3\",\n  \"id\": \"clean-2\",\n  \"article\": 24,\n  \"description\": \"Will NVIDIA's Vera Rubin next-generation AI chip platform begin shipping to customers by the end of calendar 2026?\",\n  \"outcome\": \"First shipments (initial customer deliveries / revenue recognition) of NVIDIA's Vera Rubin platform, the next-generation GPU line carrying the company's data-center value.\",\n  \"period\": \"Calendar 2026 — the item says Vera Rubin is 'in full production and could begin shipping later this year'; outcome checked at NVIDIA's fourth-quarter FY2027 report (fiscal year ending late January 2027, expected ~February 2027) that would confirm shipments in calendar 2026.\"\n },\n {\n  \"run\": \"dev-d3\",\n  \"id\": \"clean-3\",\n  \"article\": 30,\n  \"description\": \"Will the Chinese government allow Nvidia to sell its H200 (and other U.S.-approved) AI chips to Chinese commercial customers, re-opening Nvidia's China data-center revenue, or will it continue to bar Nvidia from the China market?\",\n  \"outcome\": \"Whether China permits Nvidia to sell H200/approved AI chips to Chinese customers (resumption of Nvidia China revenue), versus continued exclusion of Nvidia despite the U.S. having cleared H200 exports.\",\n  \"period\": \"NVIDIA FY2027, fiscal year ending late January 2027 (set by the reason: a pending regulatory decision is tracked to the current fiscal year-end); checked at NVIDIA's Q4 FY2027 report (~February 2027) and any Chinese regulatory announcement.\"\n },\n {\n  \"run\": \"dev-d3\",\n  \"id\": \"clean-4\",\n  \"article\": 42,\n  \"description\": \"How much will the big four AI hyperscalers (Microsoft, Amazon, Alphabet, Meta) spend in combined data center capital expenditures in calendar 2026 and 2027 — the aggregate demand pool that NVIDIA's data-center revenue depends on?\",\n  \"outcome\": \"The big four AI hyperscalers' combined data center capital expenditure for calendar 2026 (and NVIDIA's projected 2027 level), as disclosed in their earnings and capex guidance.\",\n  \"period\": \"Calendar 2026, checked against the big four hyperscalers' quarterly capex disclosures and full-year figures through their Q4 2026 reports (early 2027); the 2027 level is checked through their 2027 quarterly reports. Set from the item's 'this year'/'next year' framing relative to its 2026-07-04 publication date.\"\n },\n {\n  \"run\": \"dev-d3\",\n  \"id\": \"clean-5\",\n  \"article\": 49,\n  \"description\": \"Will Nvidia's Kyber rack-scale architecture — the rack system designed to house its Rubin Ultra chips — reach first customer shipments in 2028, rather than 2027 as previously slated or later still, and will the NVL576 eight-rack scale-up system follow it into volume?\",\n  \"outcome\": \"First customer shipments / volume availability of the Kyber NVL144 rack (144 GPUs per cabinet) and of the NVL576 eight-rack optical scale-up system that SemiAnalysis says has slipped from 2027 to 2028 on PCB-midplane manufacturability problems.\",\n  \"period\": \"Calendar 2028 — the debut date the item reports (delayed more than 12 months from the 2027 Vera Rubin Ultra launch); checked against Nvidia's shipment and product disclosures through its FY2029 Form 10-K (fiscal year ending late January 2029).\"\n },\n {\n  \"run\": \"dev-d3\",\n  \"id\": \"clean-6\",\n  \"article\": 59,\n  \"description\": \"How large will NVIDIA's supply purchase commitments be at its next annual report (FY2027 Form 10-K) — i.e., how much committed purchase volume is the company carrying into the memory and CoWoS/component supply chain, and how much of it is take-or-pay?\",\n  \"outcome\": \"The dollar amount of NVIDIA's purchase/supply commitments disclosed in the contractual obligations and purchase commitments disclosures of its FY2027 Form 10-K, compared with the $119 billion cited in this item.\",\n  \"period\": \"NVIDIA's next annual report — FY2027 Form 10-K for the fiscal year ending late January 2027, expected filed around February 2027 (set by the reason: an obligation already undertaken is tracked by its amount at the next annual report).\"\n },\n {\n  \"run\": \"dev-d3\",\n  \"id\": \"clean-7\",\n  \"article\": 59,\n  \"description\": \"How large will the custom AI ASIC (hyperscaler XPU) pool be in calendar 2027 — specifically, what will Broadcom's and Marvell's combined AI custom-silicon revenue be, and how fast is it growing relative to NVIDIA's GPU accelerator revenue?\",\n  \"outcome\": \"Broadcom's and Marvell's combined AI semiconductor/custom silicon revenue for calendar 2027, as disclosed in their quarterly reports, versus the growth of NVIDIA's data-center accelerator revenue.\",\n  \"period\": \"Calendar 2027 — checked against Broadcom's and Marvell's quarterly AI semiconductor revenue disclosures through their reports covering calendar 2027 (reported through early 2028). Set as next calendar year relative to the item's 2026-07-06 publication.\"\n },\n {\n  \"run\": \"dev-d3\",\n  \"id\": \"clean-8\",\n  \"article\": 59,\n  \"description\": \"What will memory (HBM/DRAM) contract prices be in calendar 2027 — i.e., how much will memory input costs inflate the bill of materials for NVIDIA's AI systems and pressure its gross margin or supply availability?\",\n  \"outcome\": \"The level and direction of HBM/DRAM contract prices in calendar 2027 as reported by price trackers and by the memory makers' (Micron, SK Hynix, Samsung) quarterly pricing, margin and capacity disclosures.\",\n  \"period\": \"Calendar 2027, checked against quarterly memory contract price releases and the memory makers' quarterly results through calendar 2027. Set as next calendar year relative to the item's 2026-07-06 publication.\"\n },\n {\n  \"run\": \"dev-d3\",\n  \"id\": \"clean-9\",\n  \"article\": 68,\n  \"description\": \"Will Nvidia's Rubin Ultra GPU reach first customer shipments in 2027, and in the reduced two-chiplet configuration — about half the performance of the originally planned four-die design that SemiAnalysis says was canceled on manufacturing-execution concerns — rather than the four-die version?\",\n  \"outcome\": \"First customer shipments of Nvidia's Rubin Ultra GPU generation in 2027, and whether those chips use the two-chiplet design delivering roughly half the canceled four-die design's performance.\",\n  \"period\": \"Calendar 2027 (the Rubin Ultra generation the item places around the 2027 launch, with Kyber racks housing Rubin Ultra originally slated for 2027). Checked against Nvidia's 2027 product/shipment disclosures and independent teardown/benchmark reports.\"\n },\n {\n  \"run\": \"dev-d3\",\n  \"id\": \"clean-10\",\n  \"article\": 101,\n  \"description\": \"How large will the combined revenue of named merchant AI inference-chip startups (SambaNova and Rebellions) be in calendar 2026, and how fast is it growing relative to NVIDIA's data-center accelerator revenue?\",\n  \"outcome\": \"SambaNova's and Rebellions' combined revenue for calendar 2026, as disclosed in their IPO filings or other public reports, versus NVIDIA's data-center revenue growth.\",\n  \"period\": \"Calendar 2026 — checked against SambaNova's U.S. IPO prospectus/filings (considering a 2027 IPO) and Rebellions' Kospi IPO prospectus (planned Q1/Q2 2027), which would disclose 2026 revenue.\"\n }\n][\n {\n  \"id\": \"q01\",\n  \"question\": \"What will Nvidia's total revenue be in FY2027?\",\n  \"unit\": \"USD\",\n  \"due_day\": \"2027-02-28\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"q02\",\n  \"question\": \"What Data Center segment revenue will NVIDIA report for FY2027?\",\n  \"unit\": \"USD\",\n  \"due_day\": \"2027-02-28\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"q03\",\n  \"question\": \"What non-GAAP gross margin will NVIDIA report for FY2027?\",\n  \"unit\": \"percent (75 means 75%)\",\n  \"due_day\": \"2027-02-28\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"q04\",\n  \"question\": \"How much will the four largest AI hyperscalers spend on data-center capital expenditures in calendar 2026?\",\n  \"unit\": \"USD\",\n  \"due_day\": \"2027-12-31\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"q05\",\n  \"question\": \"How will server DRAM and HBM contract prices in calendar 2027 compare with calendar 2026?\",\n  \"unit\": \"percent change 2027 vs 2026 (10 means up 10%)\",\n  \"due_day\": \"2028-01-31\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"q06\",\n  \"question\": \"What share of calendar-2026 data-center AI accelerator spending will NVIDIA hold, by the first published full-year estimate?\",\n  \"unit\": \"percent\",\n  \"due_day\": \"2027-03-31\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"q07\",\n  \"question\": \"Will Nvidia begin shipping its Rubin generation by December 31, 2026?\",\n  \"unit\": \"yes/no\",\n  \"due_day\": \"2026-12-31\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"q08\",\n  \"question\": \"Will Chinese authorities issue any authorization for Chinese companies to import Nvidia H200 chips by January 31, 2027?\",\n  \"unit\": \"yes/no\",\n  \"due_day\": \"2027-01-31\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"q09\",\n  \"question\": \"What total amount of financing commitments and capacity backstops to customers and partners will NVIDIA report outstanding at its FY2027 year-end?\",\n  \"unit\": \"USD\",\n  \"due_day\": \"2027-02-28\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"q10\",\n  \"question\": \"What non-GAAP operating margin will NVIDIA report for FY2027?\",\n  \"unit\": \"percent\",\n  \"due_day\": \"2027-02-28\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"q11\",\n  \"question\": \"What non-GAAP diluted earnings per share will NVIDIA report for FY2027?\",\n  \"unit\": \"USD per share\",\n  \"due_day\": \"2027-02-28\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"q12\",\n  \"question\": \"How much will NVIDIA spend on capital expenditures in FY2027?\",\n  \"unit\": \"USD\",\n  \"due_day\": \"2027-02-28\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"q13\",\n  \"question\": \"How much will the largest AI hyperscalers spend on data-center capital expenditures in calendar 2027?\",\n  \"unit\": \"USD\",\n  \"due_day\": \"2028-12-31\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"q14\",\n  \"question\": \"What CoWoS advanced-packaging capacity will TSMC reach by the end of calendar 2026, in wafers a month?\",\n  \"unit\": \"wafers per month\",\n  \"due_day\": \"2027-03-31\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"q15\",\n  \"question\": \"By how much will worldwide semiconductor industry revenue grow in calendar 2026 over 2025?\",\n  \"unit\": \"percent growth 2026 vs 2025\",\n  \"due_day\": \"2027-03-31\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"q16\",\n  \"question\": \"How much will cloud providers spend on custom AI silicon (ASICs) in calendar 2026?\",\n  \"unit\": \"USD\",\n  \"due_day\": \"2027-03-31\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"q17\",\n  \"question\": \"What share of China's calendar-2026 data-center AI accelerator spending will NVIDIA hold, by the first published full-year estimate?\",\n  \"unit\": \"percent\",\n  \"due_day\": \"2027-03-31\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"q18\",\n  \"question\": \"Will NVIDIA begin shipping its Rubin Ultra generation, in Kyber NVL144 racks, by December 31, 2027?\",\n  \"unit\": \"yes/no\",\n  \"due_day\": \"2027-12-31\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"q19\",\n  \"question\": \"How much revenue will NVIDIA report from standalone Vera CPUs in FY2027?\",\n  \"unit\": \"USD\",\n  \"due_day\": \"2027-02-28\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"q20\",\n  \"question\": \"How much revenue will NVIDIA report from Blackwell and Rubin products in FY2027?\",\n  \"unit\": \"USD\",\n  \"due_day\": \"2027-02-28\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"q21\",\n  \"question\": \"Will the SK Telecom AI factory built with NVIDIA GPUs begin operating by June 30, 2027?\",\n  \"unit\": \"yes/no\",\n  \"due_day\": \"2027-06-30\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"q22\",\n  \"question\": \"What will Nvidia's total revenue be in FY2028?\",\n  \"unit\": \"USD\",\n  \"due_day\": \"2028-02-28\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"q23\",\n  \"question\": \"Will NVIDIA sign a guarantee of OpenAI's Ohio data-center lease by 2027-06-30?\",\n  \"unit\": \"yes/no\",\n  \"due_day\": \"2027-06-30\"\n }\n]","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
